 <xsd:complexType name="ConversationVendorInfo">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the connection between the partner vendor system and the Service Cloud feature. For example, for Service Cloud Voice, this type contains information about the partner telephony system or Contact Center as a Service (CCaaS) system. For Bring Your Own Channel for Messaging or Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS, this type contains information about the partner messaging system or CCaaS system.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_conversationvendorinfo.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="agentSSOSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, agents can single sign-on (SSO) into their contact center using Salesforce as the identity provider (IdP). Behind the scenes, Salesforce is used as the SAML IdP in the Single Sign-On connected app for the contact center. If set to false, an IdP other than Salesforce is used or an IdP isn’t used at all. The default value is false. If this value is set to false and you want to use Salesforce as the IdP for your contact center, set this value and the namedCredentialSupported value to true and configure the service_cloud_voice.PartnerSSO interface in your Apex integration class. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="awsAccountKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The 12-digit AWS subaccount ID that’s automatically provisioned for you when Service Cloud Voice was turned on. Available in API version 55.0 and later. Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="awsRootEmail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The email address used by Salesforce to create the root user for the provisioned AWS subaccount when Service Cloud Voice was turned on. Available in API version 55.0 and later. Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="awsTenantVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The version number of the SVCTenantStack AWS CloudFormation stack that’s deployed. The stack is deployed in AWS region &quot;us-east-1&quot;. Available in API version 55.0 and later. Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="bridgeComponent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The Lightning component used to communicate between the telephony or messaging system and other Lightning components. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="clientAuthMode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The client authentication mode. Values are: Custom Mixed SSO Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ClientAuthMode (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="connectorUrl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The URL that hosts your Service Cloud Voice or Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS connector. This value could be a Visualforce page or a public URL. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customConfig" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The foreign key to the CustomEntityDefinition, which contains partner-specific custom settings. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customIcon" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>ID of the static resource used to identify the contact center integration, such as a Contact Center as a Service (CCaaS) provider logo. The static resource must be in SVG format. This field is optional. Available in API version 62.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customLoginUrl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The URL that hosts your telephony system or CCaaS system login page. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The unique name of the type in the API.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="einsteinConversationInsightsSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, Einstein Conversation Insights is turned on. The default value is false. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="integrationClass" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The foreign key to the partner Apex class implementing supported interfaces. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="integrationClassName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Deprecated in API version 53.0. Don&apos;t set this field. Instead, use integrationClass. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="intelligenceSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, Salesforce ingests real-time signals sent from a partner telephony system. If set to false, Salesforce won&apos;t ingest real-time intelligence signals from a partner telephony system. The default value is false. Available in API version 59.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isTaxCompliant" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the Amazon tax settings for the AWS subaccount provisioned for Service Cloud Voice have been confirmed (true). The default value is false. Available in API version 55.0 and later.Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyProvisioningSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, key provisioning and renewal are automated. The default value is false. Available in API version 54.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The partner vendor&apos;s display name as it appears in the UI. This name appears in several places in the UI, so include the partner vendor name for easy identification. For Service Cloud Voice, this label also represents the telephony provider name in the contact center record. For Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect, this field is always set to Service Cloud Voice.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="namedCredential" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A sample-named credential that can be used for Apex callouts to the partner system. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="namedCredentialSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A sample-named credential that can be used for Apex callouts to the partner system. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="partnerContactCenterListSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, enables the customer to select one contact center from a list of multiple contact centers to connect with Salesforce. The default value is false. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="partnerPhoneNumbersSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, displays a list of phone numbers used to create contact center channels. The default value is false. Available in API version 54.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="partnerTransferDestinationsSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, allows Salesforce to fetch contact center queues so that Salesforce and contact center queues can be mapped. The default value is false. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="queueManagementSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, support queue management. The default value is false. Available in API version 56.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="serverAuthMode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Deprecated in API 53.0. Server authentication mode. Set this value to None. Values are: None OAuth Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServerAuthMode (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="telephonySettingsComponent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the Lightning Web Component (LWC) that is used to display additional agent settings in the Omni-Channel widget. This value is in the format mynamespace:componentName, where mynamespace is the namespace associated with the Service Cloud Voice package that was created, and componentName is the FQDN of the Lightning component. Available in API version 54.0 and later. Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="unifiedRoutingSupported_Beta" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether unified routing is supported (true) or not supported (false) for voice calls in voice channels. The default value is false. Once this value is set to true, it can’t be changed to false. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Applies to the following implementation: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="universalCallRecordingAccessSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, Universal Call Recording Access is turned on. The default value is false. If this value is set to false and you want to turn on Universal Call Recording, set this value to true and configure the service_cloud_voice.RecordingMediaProvider interface in your Apex integration class. Available in API version 54.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userSyncingSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, supports automated user syncing whenever a user is added to or removed from a contact center. The default value is false. Available in API version 53.0 and later. Applies to the following implementations: Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect Bring Your Own Channel for CCaaS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="vendorType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The Service Cloud feature the partner vendor supports.Possible values are: Amazon_Connect — For Service Cloud Voice with Amazon Connect. BringYourOwnChannelPartner — For Bring Your Own Channel for Messaging. Available in API version 60.0 and later. BringYourOwnContactCenter — For Bring Your Own Channel for Contact Center as a Service (CCaaS). Available in API version 60.0 and later. ServiceCloudVoicePartner — For Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony or Service Cloud Voice with Partner Telephony from Amazon Connect. Available in API version 53.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ConversationVendorType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CorsWhitelistOrigin">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an origin in the CORS allowlist.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_corswhitelistorigin.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="urlPattern" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A URL pattern for the origin. The origin URL pattern must include the HTTPS protocol and a domain name, and can include a port. The wildcard character (*) is supported and must be in front of a second-level domain name. For example, https://*.example.com adds all subdomains of example.com to the allowlist. Google Chrome™ and Mozilla® Firefox® browser extensions are also allowed as resources in API version 53 and later. Chrome extensions must use the prefix chrome-extension:// and 32 characters without digits or capital letters, for example chrome-extension://abdkkegmcbiomijcbdaodaflgehfffed. Firefox extensions must use the prefix moz-extension:// and an 8-4-4-4-12 format of small alphanumeric characters, for example moz-extension://1234ab56-78c9-1df2-3efg-4567891hi1j2. The origin URL pattern can be an IP address. But an IP address and a domain that resolve to the same address aren’t the same origin, and you must add them to the CORS allowlist as separate entries.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: String</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CountriesAndStates">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the configuration of country/territory and state picklists. Use the AddressSettings component type to configure state and country/territory data in your organization so that you can convert text-based values into standard picklist values. To convert your state and country/territory values, from Setup, enter State and Country/Territory Picklists in the Quick Find box, then select State and Country/Territory Picklists.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_addresssettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="countries" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The countries and territories available in picklists.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Country[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Country">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>This metadata type provides the definition for a country/territory in a picklist.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_addresssettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines whether the value is available in the API.After you enable state and country/territory picklists in your Salesforce organization, you can’t set the active status to false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="integrationValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A customizable text value that is linked to a state or country/territory code. Integration values for standard states, countries, and territories default to the full ISO-standard state, country, and territory names. Integration values function similarly to the API names of custom fields and objects. Configuring integration values allows integrations that you set up before enabling state and country/territory picklists to continue to work.If you don’t specify integration values before enabling state and country/territory picklists in your organization, records use the default value provided by Salesforce. If you change integration values later, records created or updated from that point on use your edited values.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isoCode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ISO-standard code populates this field when you issue a retrieve() call. This field is read only in the API but you can edit the label in Setup. You can’t edit the isoCode of standard states, countries, and territories.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The label is what users see in picklists in Salesforce. This field is read only in the API but you can edit the label in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="orgDefault" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Sets a country or territory as the default value for new records in the Salesforce organization.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="standard" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Standard states and countries are states and countries that are included with Salesforce. You can’t edit the standard attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="states" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The states or provinces that are part of the country or territory.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: State[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="visible" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Makes the state, country, or territory available to users in Salesforce. States, countries, or territories that are visible must also be active.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CtxAttrHydrationCtx">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the queries that fetch data for a chosen attribute from the input schema for context-to-context mapping.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_contextdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="contextQueryAttribute" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Attribute in context definition that&apos;s the source of context hydration.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inheritedFrom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the parent context attribute hydration detail that&apos;s used to derive the current context attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomApplication">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>CustomApplication represents a custom or standard application. In API version 29.0 and earlier, CustomApplication represents only a custom application. An application is a list of tab references, with a description and a logo. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="actionOverrides" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents an action override for an application. Use it to create, update, edit, or delete action overrides.This field is available for Lightning Experience in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppActionOverride[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="brand" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The color scheme and logo used for the app.This field is available for Lightning Experience in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppBrand</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="consoleConfig" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents configuration settings for a Salesforce console app.This field is available in API version 42.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceCloudConsoleConfig</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultLandingTab" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The fullName of a standard tab or custom tab that opens when this application is selected.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The optional description text of the application.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="formFactors" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the form factors for which the app is visible for Lightning Experience. Valid values are: Null (no value)—For a desktop using Salesforce Classic Small—For a mobile device using the Salesforce mobile app Medium—Reserved for future use Large—For a desktop using Lightning Experience This field is available in API version 38.0 and later. As of API version 38.0, formFactors is set to Large for existing Salesforce Classic apps, except for Salesforce Classic consoles. Salesforce Classic apps installed from packages created before API version 38.0 also have formFactors set to Large. For Salesforce Classic apps in packages created with API 38.0 or later, you must set formFactors to Large for Salesforce Classic apps to appear in the Lightning Experience desktop. As of API version 47.0, the Small value is supported for Lightning apps. The formFactors field can be set to Small or Large for Lightning apps, and it can be set to Null or Large for Salesforce Classic apps.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FormFactor (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isNavAutoTempTabsDisabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the navigation automatically creates temporary tabs settings. Applies only to Lightning apps with standard navigation. Available in API version 43.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isNavPersonalizationDisabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether navigation personalization is disabled. Applies only to Lightning apps. Available in API version 43.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isNavTabPersistenceDisabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether workspace tabs are cleared for each new console session (true) or not (false). Applies only to Lightning apps with console navigation. Available in API version 54.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isServiceCloudConsole" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if the application is a Salesforce Classic console app. For Lightning Experience console apps, this field is null and the navType field is set to Console.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the application.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="logo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The optional reference to the image document for a Salesforce app or Salesforce console app.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="navType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Not updateable. Indicates the type of navigation the app uses. The value Standard is for a Lightning app with standard navigation. The value Console is for a Lightning app with console navigation.This field is available in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: NavType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="preferences" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the preferences for a Salesforce Classic console app. All of the AppPreferences fields are required.This field is available in API version 42.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppPreferences</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="profileActionOverrides" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of the Lightning Experience record page ProfileActionOverrides that are assigned to this custom app. When a user invokes the custom app, a matching ProfileActionOverride assignment takes precedence over existing overrides for the record page specified in ActionOverride. You can override a record page for the custom app by record type and profile.In API version 45.0 and later, you can override a home page for the custom app by profile.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppProfileActionOverride[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="setupExperience" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of Setup experience associated with the app. Valid values are: all—Represents the full Setup tree. essentials—Represents the Essentials Setup tree, which contains a subset of Setup items configured for Essentials edition. service—Represents the Service Setup tree, which contains a subset of Setup items configured for Service Console. A null value is equivalent to all. Previous valid values AllSetup, ServiceSetup, and EssentialsSetup have been deprecated. This field is available in API version 39.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subscriberTabs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the list of tabs appended by a subscriber to a Lightning app installed from a managed package. Records in a subscriber tab always open as primary tabs.This field is available in API version 41.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="tabs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of tabs included in this application. In API version 12.0, the fullName for built-in tabs like Home, Account, and Reports, is the name of the tab (Home, for example). In API version 13.0 and later, built-in tabs are prefixed with standard-. For example, to reference the Account tab you would use standard-Account.In API version 42.0, this field was renamed from tab to tabs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="uiType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Not updateable. Identifies the type of custom app. The value is: Aloha for Salesforce Classic Lightning for Lightning Experience This field is available in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UiType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="utilityBar" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of the utility bar associated with this app. We recommend assigning a utility bar to only one Lightning App, because utility bars are shared. Sharing means that if you change the utility bar in one app, it automatically changes in all apps associated with it. This field is available in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="workspaceConfig" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents how records open in a Salesforce console app. Required if isServiceCloudConsole is true. In API version 42.0, this field was renamed to workspaceConfig from workspaceMappings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppWorkspaceConfig</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomApplicationComponent">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a custom console component (Visualforce page) assigned to a CustomApplication that is marked as a Salesforce console. Custom console components extend the capabilities of Salesforce console apps. See Customize a Console with Custom Components in Salesforce Classic in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplicationcomponent.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="buttonIconUrl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The address of a page that hosts an icon for the button.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="buttonStyle" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The inline style used to define how the button looks.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="buttonText" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The label on the button used to launch the custom console component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="buttonWidth" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The pixel width of the button displayed in the Salesforce console.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="height" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The pixel height of the window used to display the custom console component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isHeightFixed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether users can change the custom console component height (false) or not (true).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isHidden" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the custom console component is hidden from users (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isWidthFixed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether users can change the component width (false) or not (true).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="visualforcePage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the Visualforce page that represents the custom console component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="width" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The pixel width of the window used to display the custom console component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomApplicationTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>CustomApplicationTranslation contains details for a custom application translation. For more details, see CustomApplication.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The optional description text of the application translation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The translated custom application name. Maximum of 765 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the custom application.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomFeedFilter">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a custom feed filter that limits the feed view to feeds from the Cases object. The custom feed filter shows only feed items that satisfy the criteria specified in the CustomFeedFilter definition. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customfeedfilter.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="criteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The criterion that defines which feed items are shown when the filter is applied. The feed filter displays all feed items that satisfy the criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FeedFilterCriterion []</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the custom feed filter. For example, specify what feed items that filter shows.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API label of the custom feed filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value. It currently has no impact.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a field. Use this metadata type to create, update, or delete custom field definitions on standard, custom, and external objects or standard field definitions on standard objects.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/customfield.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="businessOwnerGroup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the group associated with this field. The business owner group understands the importance of the field’s data to your company, and can be responsible for determining the minimum security classification. This field is available in API version 45.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: reference</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="businessOwnerUser" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the person associated with this field. The business owner understands the importance of the field’s data to your company, and can be responsible for determining the minimum security classification. This field is available in API version 45.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: reference</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="businessStatus" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is in use. Valid values include: Active DeprecateCandidate Hidden This field is available in API version 45.0 and later</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="caseSensitive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is case-sensitive (true) or not (false).For indirect lookup relationship fields on external objects, this attribute affects how this custom field’s values are matched against the values of the referenceTargetField.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="complianceGroup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the compliance acts, definitions, or regulations related to the field’s data. Valid values include: CCPA COPPA GDPR HIPAA PCI PII This field is available in API version 47.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: multipicklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customDataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Deprecated in the Spring ‘19 (API version 45.0) release.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, represents the default value of the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="deleteConstraint" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Provides deletion options for lookup relationships. Valid values are: Cascade—Deletes the lookup record as well as associated lookup fields. Restrict—Prevents the record from being deleted if it&apos;s in a lookup relationship. SetNull—This value is the default. If the lookup record is deleted, the lookup field is cleared. For more information on lookup relationships, see &quot;Object Relationships&quot; in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DeleteConstraint (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="deprecated" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reserved for future use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Description of the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="displayFormat" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The display format.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="displayLocationInDecimal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates how the geolocation values of a custom Location field appear in the user interface. If true, the geolocation values appear in decimal notation. If false, the geolocation values appear as degrees, minutes, and seconds.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="elementType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reserved for future use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ElementType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="encrypted" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This entry is about Shield Platform Encryption, not Classic Encryption. Indicates whether this field is encrypted (true) or not (false). This field is available in API version 34.0 through 43.0.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="encryptionScheme" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This entry is about Shield Platform Encryption, not Classic Encryption. For encrypted fields, determines which encryption scheme a field takes. Valid values are CaseInsensitiveDeterministicEncryption CaseSensitiveDeterministicEncryption None ProbabilisticEncryption This field is available in API version 44.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: EncryptionScheme (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalDeveloperName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Available only for external objects. Name of the table column on the external data source that maps to this custom field in Salesforce. Corresponds to External Column Name in the user interface. This field is available in API version 32.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalId" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is an external ID field (true) or not (false). This property is returned only if the custom field data type is AutoNumber, Email, Number, or Text.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="formula" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, represents a formula on the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="formulaTreatBlanksAs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates how to treat blanks in a formula. Valid values are: BlankAsBlank and BlankAsZero.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TreatBlanksAs (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Inherited from Metadata, this field is defined in the WSDL for this metadata type. It must be specified when creating, updating, or deleting. See createMetadata() to see an example of this field specified for a call.This value can&apos;t be null.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="globalPicklist" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>(This field is available in API version 37.0 only and removed from later versions.) If this custom field is a picklist that’s based on a global picklist, globalPicklist is the name of the global picklist whose value set this picklist inherits. A custom picklist that’s based on a global picklist is restricted. You can only add or remove values by editing the global picklist.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string.</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="indexed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if the field is indexed. If this field is unique or the externalId is set true, the isIndexed value is set to true. This field has been deprecated as of API version 14.0 and is only provided for backward compatibility.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inlineHelpText" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the content of field-level help. For more information, see &quot;Define Field-Level Help&quot; in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isFilteringDisabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Available only for external objects. Indicates whether the custom field is available in filters. This field is available in API version 32.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isSortingDisabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Available only for external objects. Indicates whether the custom field is sortable. This field is available in API version 32.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Label for the field. You can&apos;t update the label for standard picklist fields, such as the Industry field for accounts.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="length" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Length of the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lookupFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a lookup filter. This metadata type is used to create, update, or delete lookup filter definitions. This component has been removed as of API version 30.0 and is only available in previous API versions. The metadata associated with a lookup filter is now represented by the lookupFilter field in the CustomField component. This field is available in API version 30.0 and later. LookupFilter isn&apos;t supported on the article type object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: LookupFilter</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="maskChar" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This page is about Classic Encryption, not Shield Platform Encryption. For encrypted fields, specifies the character to be used as a mask. Valid values are: asterisk X For more information on encrypted fields, see Classic Encryption for Custom Fields in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: EncryptedFieldMaskChar (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="maskType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This page is about Classic Encryption, not Shield Platform Encryption. For encrypted text fields, specifies the format of the masked and unmasked characters in the field. Valid values are: all—All characters in the field are hidden. This option is equivalent to the Mask All Characters option in Salesforce. creditCard—The first 12 characters are hidden and the last four display. This option is equivalent to the Credit Card Number option in Salesforce. lastFour—All characters are hidden but the last four display. This option is equivalent to the Last Four Characters Clear option in Salesforce. nino—All characters are hidden. Salesforce automatically inserts spaces after each pair of characters if the field contains nine characters. This option is equivalent to the National Insurance Number option in Salesforce. sin—All characters are hidden but the last four display. This option is equivalent to the Social Insurance Number option in Salesforce. ssn—The first five characters are hidden and the last four display. This option is equivalent to the Social Security Number option in Salesforce. For more information on encrypted fields, see &quot;Classic Encryption for Custom Fields&quot; in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: EncryptedFieldMaskType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="picklist" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>(Deprecated. Use this field in API version 37.0 and earlier only. In later versions, use valueSet instead.) If specified, the field is a picklist, and this field enumerates the picklist values and labels.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="populateExistingRows" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether existing rows are going to be populated (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="precision" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The precision for number values. Precision is the number of digits in a number. For example, the number 256.99 has a precision value of 5.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="referenceTo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, indicates a reference this field has to another object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relationshipLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Label for the relationship.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relationshipName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, indicates the value for one-to-many relationships. For example, in the object MyObject that had a relationship to YourObject, the relationship name can be YourObjects.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relationshipOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This field is valid for all master-detail relationships, but the value is only non-zero for junction objects. A junction object has two master-detail relationships, and is analogous to an association table in a many-to-many relationship. Junction objects must define one parent object as primary (0), the other as secondary (1). The definition of primary or secondary affects delete behavior and inheritance of look and feel, and record ownership for junction objects. For more information, see Salesforce Help. 0 or 1 are the only valid values, and 0 is always the value for objects that aren&apos;t junction objects.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="reparentableMasterDetail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the child records in a master-detail relationship on a custom object can be reparented to different parent records. The default value is false.This field is available in API version 25.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="required" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field requires a value on creation (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="scale" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The scale for the field. Scale is the number of digits to the right of the decimal point in a number. For example, the number 256.99 has a scale of 2.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="securityClassification" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the sensitivity of the data contained in the field. Valid values include: Public Internal Confidential Restricted MissionCritical This field is available in API version 45.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="startingNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, indicates the starting number for the field. When you create records, Starting Number’s value increments to store the number that will be assigned to the next auto-number field created. You can’t retrieve the starting number of an auto-number field through Metadata API. To specify a Starting Number while deploying, add a startingNumber tag for your field to your package.xml file. For example: &lt;startingNumber&gt;42&lt;/startingNumber&gt; If you deploy without specifying a Starting Number value in your package.xml file, the default starting number for standard fields is 0. The default starting number for custom fields is 1.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stripMarkup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Set to true to remove markup, or false to preserve markup. Used when converting a rich text area to a long text area.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="summaryFilterItems" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the set of filter conditions for this field if it&apos;s a summary field. This field is summed on the child if the filter conditions are met.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FilterItem[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="summaryForeignKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the master-detail field on the child that defines the relationship between the parent and the child.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="summaryOperation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the type of sum operation to be performed. Valid values are: Count Min Max Sum</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SummaryOperations (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="trackFeedHistory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is enabled for feed tracking (true) or not (false). To set this field to true, the enableFeeds field on the associated CustomObject must also be true. For more information, see &quot;Customize Chatter Feed Tracking&quot; in Salesforce Help.This field is available in API version 18.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="trackHistory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether history tracking is enabled for the field (true) or not (false). Also available for standard object fields (picklist and lookup fields only) in API version 30.0 and later.To set trackHistory to true, the enableHistory field on the associated standard or custom object must also be true. For more information, see &quot;Field History Tracking&quot; in Salesforce Help. Field history tracking isn’t available for external objects.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="trackTrending" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether historical trending data is captured for the field (true) or not (false). An object is enabled for historical trending if this attribute is true for at least one field. Available in API version 29.0 and later.For more information, see &quot;Report on Historical Changes&quot; in Salesforce Help.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="trueValueIndexed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Only relevant for a checkbox field. If set, true values are built into the index. This field has been deprecated as of API version 14.0 and is only provided for backward compatibility.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the field type for the field. Valid values are enumerated in FieldType.For standard fields on standard objects, the type field is optional. This field is included for some standard field types, such as Picklist or Lookup, but not for others. The type field is included for custom fields.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FieldType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="unique" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is unique (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="valueSet" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the set of values that make up a picklist on a custom field. Each value is defined as a CustomValue. If this custom field is a picklist that uses a global value set, valueSet is the name of the global value set whose values this picklist inherits. A custom picklist that uses a global value set is restricted. You can only add or remove values by editing the global value set. A ValueSet component has either a valueSetDefinition or a valueName specified, but never both. This field is available in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ValueSet</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="visibleLines" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the number of lines displayed for the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="writeRequiresMasterRead" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Sets the minimum sharing access level required on the primary record to create, edit, or delete child records. This field applies only to master-detail or junction object custom field types. true—Allows users with Read access to the primary record permission to create, edit, or delete child records. This setting makes sharing less restrictive. false—Allows users with Read/Write access to the primary record permission to create, edit, or delete child records. This setting is more restrictive than true, and is the default value. For junction objects, the most restrictive access from the two parents is enforced. For example, if you set to true on both master-detail fields, but users have Read access to one primary record and Read/Write access to the other primary record, users aren&apos;t able to create, edit, or delete child records.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomFieldDisplay">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the view type assigned to product attribute custom fields. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customfielddisplay.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="displayType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The view type of the product attribute custom fields. Values are: ColorSwatch Dropdown Pill</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomFieldDisplayType​ (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The primary label for this object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomHelpMenuItems">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Items included in the custom section. Specify up to 15 items.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customhelpmenusection.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="linkURL" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The URL for the resource.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the resource. Specify up to 100 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The order of the item within the custom section. Valid values are 1 through 15.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomHelpMenuSection">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the section of the Lightning Experience help menu that the admin added to display custom, org-specific help resources for the org. The custom section contains help resources added by the admin. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customhelpmenusection.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="customHelpMenuItems" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Items included in the custom section. Specify up to 15 items.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomHelpMenuItems[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the custom section. Only one custom section can be added to the Lightning Experience help menu. Specify up to 80 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomHttpHeaders">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a custom HTTP header used with OData 2.0 or OData 4.0 connectors. Available in API version 43.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_externaldatasource.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A text description of the header field’s purpose.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the custom HTTP header is available to use (true) or unavailable (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomIndex">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an index used to increase the speed of queries.This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customindex.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="allowNullValues" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether null values are allowed in the index (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="booleanIndexedValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether boolean fields are indexed (true) or not (false). Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomLabelTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>CustomLabelTranslation contains details for a custom label translation. For more details, see CustomLabels.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The translated custom label name. Maximum of 765 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The custom label name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomNotificationType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a custom notification type.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customnotificationtype.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="customNotifTypeName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies a notification type name. Maximum number of characters: 80.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies a general description of the notification type, which is displayed with the notification type name. Maximum number of characters: 255.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="desktop" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the desktop delivery channel is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the label for the notification type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="mobile" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the mobile delivery channel is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="slack" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reserved for future use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomPageWebLinkTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>CustomPageWebLinkTranslation contains details for a translation of a web link defined in a home page component. For more details, see CustomPageWebLink.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The translated web link.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the web link.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomShortcut">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents custom keyboard shortcuts assigned to a Salesforce console app in Salesforce Classic. Before you can create custom shortcuts, a developer must define the shortcut’s action with the addEventListener() method in the Salesforce Console Integration Toolkit. You can’t create keyboard shortcuts for actions performed outside of the console. Available in API version 28.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="action" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The action performed in the console when a user presses the keyboard shortcut.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the keyboard shortcut is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyCommand" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The combination of keys a user presses to trigger the keyboard shortcut. Keyboard shortcuts aren’t case-sensitive, but they display as uppercase on setup pages in the Salesforce user interface so that they’re easier to read.Each key command can include up to four modifier keys followed by one non-modifier key. Modifier and non-modifier keys are separated by the + key. Modifier keys can occur in any order, but you must place non-modifier keys at the end of the key command sequence. For example, SHIFT+CTRL+ALT+META +A. Valid modifier keys are: SHIFT CTRL ALT META (represents the COMMAND key on Macs) Valid non-modifier keys are letters A through Z and numbers 0 through 9. Other valid keys are: TAB ENTER PAUSE/BREAK CAPS LOCK ESC SPACE PAGE UP PAGE DOWN END HOME LEFT ARROW UP ARROW RIGHT ARROW DOWN ARROW PRINT SCREEN INSERT DELETE RIGHT WINDOW NUMPAD 0 NUMPAD 1 NUMPAD 2 NUMPAD 3 NUMPAD 4 NUMPAD 5 NUMPAD 6 NUMPAD 7 NUMPAD 8 NUMPAD 9 MULTIPLY ADD SUBTRACT DECIMAL POINT DIVIDE F1 F2 F3 F4 F5 F6 F7 F8 F9 F10 F11 F12 NUM LOCK SCROLL LOCK ; = , — . / ‘ [ ] \ &apos;</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The optional description text for the keyboard shortcut.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="eventName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Code available to developers who want to add custom shortcut functions to the console via the Salesforce Console Integration Toolkit.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomTabTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>CustomTabTranslation contains details for a translation of a custom tab. For more details, see CustomTab.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The translated custom tab name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The custom tab name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomerDataPlatformSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an org&apos;s Data 360 settings.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customerdataplatformsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableCustomerDataPlatform" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether an org has Data 360 enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DashboardMobileSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>These fields are deprecated. Represents your organization&apos;s Mobile Dashboards iPad app settings.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_mobilesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableDashboardIPadApp" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Mobile Dashboards iPad app has been enabled for your organization (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataConnectorIngestApi">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the connection information specific to Ingestion API.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dataconnectoringestapi.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. UI label of the Ingestion API Connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the Ingestion API Connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataConnectorS3">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the connection information specific to Amazon S3.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dataconnectors3.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="fileNameWildcard" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. File or Wildcard (*) to be used when finding files.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="importFromDirectory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Path from the directory to where files are located.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The UI name for the S3 data connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="s3BucketName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The Amazon S3 Name of the Bucket.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataPackageKitDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the top-level Data Kit container definition. Content objects can be added after the Data Kit is defined.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datapackagekitdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dataKitType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the type of data kit created. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Valid values are: Default Sandbox</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataKitSource" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the data source in the updated data kit. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the data kit.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Represents the name of the application. Can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters and must be unique in your org. It must begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isDeployed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Data Kit content is deployed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the Data Kit is enabled.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Label that identifies the AI application throughout the Salesforce user interface.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versionNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Auto incremented version number.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSpaceDefinitionDevName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Data space name used to create the data kit. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="deploymentOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Deployment order of components that are added to the data kit. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataSource">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Used to represent the system where the data was sourced. This object is always needed when creating a Data Stream Definition.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datasource.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The UI name for the Data Source.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="prefix" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Prefix for the Data Source to make Data Source Object records unique.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataSourceBundleDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the bundle of streams that a user adds to a data kit.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datasourcebundledefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dataPlatform" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the connector type that the streams in the bundle belong to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the associated data source bundle. This field is available in API version 53.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="icon" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The icon used in the deployment flow. This field is available in API version 53.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isMultiDeploymentSupported" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if the bundle can be deployed multiple times or not. Default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the name of the bundle.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="bundleVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the version of the bundle. This field is available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataSourceField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the details of a data source field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datasourcefield.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="datatype" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the data type of the field: text, number, or date.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dateFormat" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The date format of date, time, date/time fields.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="definitionCreationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Describes whether this object was added by the user or as part of a standard taxonomy. Available in API version 62.0 and later. Valid values are: Activation_Audience (Reserved for internal use only) ADG Activation_Audience. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Bridge Calculated_Insight CG_Audience Chunk Curated Custom Derived Directory_Table External Ml_Prediction Segment_Membership Semantic Standard System Transform Vector_Embedding</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DefinitionCreationType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalDataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of data in the external system. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the object in the external system. This is different from the developer name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isDataRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, data is required. Default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isEventDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, an event date is required. Default value is false. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isFormula" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, a formula is required. Default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isRecordModified" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, the system tracks the modification date of the record. Default value is false. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyQualifierName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contains the developer name of the keyQualifier field. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="length" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Length of a string column.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Field label.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="precision" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The total number of digits in a number including decimal points. Used for currency and for numeric accuracy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="primaryIndexOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If supplied, indicates that this field is part of the primary key. The number value indicates the order of attributes if it’s a compound primary key. A missing value means that this field isn’t part of the primary key.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="scale" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The number of digits to the right of the decimal point. Used for currency and for numeric accuracy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The sequence of this source schema.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="srcKeyQualifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contains a reference to the source key qualifier record. The source key is the MktDataLakeSrcKeyQualifer metadata type. Available in API version 55.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="usageTag" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if the field is a key qualifier field. Available in API version 55.0 and later.Values are: KEY_QUALIFIER—The field is used as a key qualifier field. NONE—The field isn’t used as a key qualifier field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: usageTag (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versionNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The version of the data source object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataSourceObject">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the object from where the data was sourced.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datasourceobject.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="accelerationEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Acceleration of data stream processing. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Possible values are: Yes No</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AccelerationEnabled (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="additionalDLOInfoJson" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Additional information about the Directory Table data lake object (DLO), such as the directory path and file pattern.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="creationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether this object was added by the user or as part of a standard taxonomy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataConnection" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The source data connector for the Directory Table DLO.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSource" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The system where the data was sourced.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dmoDeveloperName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of the Directory Table data model object (DMO).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dmoLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The UI name of the Directory Table DMO.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalDatabaseName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the external database for the data source object. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalObjectName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The external data source object. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalRecordIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The identifier for the data source.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalSchemaName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the schema within the external database. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The UI name for the data source object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The category of the data source object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The object type. Possible values are: API Object Table</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataObjectType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of the source object for the data source object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="storageType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of storage used for data source object. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Possible values are: External Local</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StorageType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="templateVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The version number of the data source object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataSrcDataModelFieldMap">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the entity that is used for storing the design time bundle level mappings for the data source fields and data model fields.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datasrcdatamodelfieldmap.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the name of the entity.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versionNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the version number of the entity.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataStreamDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Contains data ingestion information such as connection, API, and file retrieval settings.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datastreamdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="areHeadersIncludedInFile" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, headers are included in the file if this is a single file stream.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="bulkIngest" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, files are aggregated before data is ingested if the file names contain a wildcard. For example, profiles*.csv.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="definitionCreationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Enum tracks the source of an object or field creation. Valid values are: Custom Standard Valid values available in API version 62.0 and later are: ADG Calculated_Insight CG_Audience Chunk Directory_Table External Semantic Transform Vector_Embedding</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataConnector" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Describe whether this data stream definition was created by a customer or by an internal system.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataConnectorType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ingestion data source. Valid values are: ACCOUNTENGAGEMENT AwsS3 AzureBlob BIG_QUERY CuratedEntity DataCloud ExternalPlatform GoogleCloudStorage IngestApi REDSHIFT SalesforceCommerceCloud SalesforceDotCom SalesforceInteractionStudio SalesforceMarketingCloud SFTP Snowflake StreamingApp UPLOAD</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataExtensionIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For a Marketing Cloud data extension, the unique identifier.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataExtractMethods" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Describes how to identify the data to be extracted. Valid values include: DATETIME_CDC FULL_REFRESH NUMERIC_CDC BINARY_CDC (reserved for future use)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataImportDataExtractMethods (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataPlatDataSetBundle" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Identifies which data set bundle this definition was created from. Useful in cases where the same item can be configured across data connections.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataPlatformDataSet" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description is provided by the developer.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataPlatformDataSetItemName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the Data Platform Set Item.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSource" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A reference to the data source from which the data originated. This is usually the API name or a unique system identifier, such as the enterprise ID (EID) of the customer in the format MC_&lt;EID&gt;. Example: MCEnterprise or MC_12345.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A description of the data stream definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fileNameWildcard" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>File or wildcard (*) used when finding files.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="internalOrganization" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the internal organization.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isLimitedToNewFiles" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, file retrieval is limited to new files.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isMissingFileFailure" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, treat the case of missing files as a failure.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. UI label for this data stream definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="mktDataLakeObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Reference to the landing entity (target) where data will be stored.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="mktDataTranObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reference to the object that’s used to transport information from the source to a landing entity (target).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataStreamTemplate">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the data stream that a user adds to a data kit.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_datastreamtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dataConnectionSourceParameters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Input representation for the data connection source parameters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectionParamTmpl[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSourceBundleDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Reference to the bundle to which this template belongs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSourceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Reference to the Data Source Objects (DSOs). A DSO represents the object from where the data was sourced.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="filterCriteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Filter applied to the data stream before the information is sent to Data Cloud.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name assigned to the data stream template.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Category of the Data Model Object (DMO).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshDayOfMonth" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The duration of the day of the month after which the data stream must be refreshed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshDayOfWeek" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The duration of the day of the week after which the data stream must be refreshed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshFrequency" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The frequency with which the datastream must be refreshed. Possible values are: Batch NONE MINUTES_15 MINUTES_30 MINUTES_5 HOURLY DAILY WEEKLY MONTHLY NOT_APPLICABLE STREAMING Possible values available in API version 64.0 and later are: EVERY_12_HOURS EVERY_4_HOURS</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataImportRefreshFrequency (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshHours" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The duration after which the datastream must be refreshed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshMode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The mode of refresh. Possible values are: FULL_REFRESH UPSERT INCREMENTAL REPLACE NEAR_REAL_TIME_INCREMENTAL NOT_APPLICABLE PARTIAL_UPDATE STREAMING</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataImportRefreshMode (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshStartDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:date">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The date to retrieve data based on the refresh frequency data. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: date</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceObjectName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the source object from which data is streamed. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="streamType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of data stream. Available in API version 62.0 and later. Possible values are: DIRECT_ACCESS DIRECT_ACCESS_ACCELERATED INGEST</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StreamType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="streamingAppDataConnectorType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The connector app for data streaming. Available in API version 63.0 and later. Possible values are: MobileApp WebApp</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: streamingAppDataConnectorType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="templateVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The version number of the template. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionMatrixDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a definition of a decision matrix.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisionmatrixdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Describes a decision matrix definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="groupKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A key for grouping matrix rows in different versions, such as a geographic region or a product code.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The UI label of a decision matrix definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="processType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The process type that uses the expression set rule. Valid values are: Bre GpaCalculation InsuranceClaimProcessing—Available in API version 65.0 and later. ItServiceManagement—Available in API version 65.0 and later. PlanCostCalculation RatingDiscovery StudentInformationSystem—Available in API version 65.0 and later. StudentSuccess When Business Rules Engine is enabled for a Salesforce instance, the default value is &apos;Bre’. Other usage types may be available to you depending on your industry solution and permission sets. Available in API version 59.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ExpsSetProcessType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subGroupKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A subgroup key for grouping matrix rows in different versions, such as a geographic region or a product code. For example, if the groupKey is Country, the subGroupKey can be State or Province.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of a decision matrix. Valid values are: Grouped Standard</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents an array of decision matrix version definitions in a decision matrix. This array must contain at least one version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixDefinitionVersion[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionMatrixDefinitionVersion">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a definition of a decision matrix version.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisionmatrixdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="columns" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents an array of columns in a decision matrix definition version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixDefinitionVersionColumn​​[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="decisionMatrixDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The full name of a decision matrix version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="endDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:dateTime">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The date until which a decision matrix definition version is available for use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: dateTime</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="groupKeyValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The value of the groupKey for a decision matrix definition version. For example, if the groupKey is Country, the groupKeyValue can be United States.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The UI label of a decision matrix definition version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rank" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The rank of the Decision Matrix Definition Version. When more than one enabled version matches a decision matrix call, and the start date time to end date time spans overlap, the version with the highest rank is chosen. Available in API version 64.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="startDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:dateTime">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The date from when a decision matrix definition version is available for use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: dateTime</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="status" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the status of a decision matrix definition version. Valid values are: Active Draft Inactive InvalidDraft Obsolete</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixDefStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subGroupKeyValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The value of the subgroup key for a decision matrix definition version. For example, if the subGroupKey is State or Province, the subGroupKeyValue can be California.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versionNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The version number of a decision matrix definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionMatrixDefinitionVersionColumn">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a definition of a column in a decision matrix definition version.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisionmatrixdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="columnType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies whether a column is for an input or output. Valid values are: Input Output</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixColumnType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of data that’s stored in a column. Valid values are: Boolean Currency Number NumberRange Percent Text TextRange</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionMatrixDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="displaySequence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Represents the position of a column in the column order.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isWildcardColumn" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies whether a column stores a wildcard value (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The full name of a decision matrix definition version column.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rangeValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of values that define range boundaries.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="wildcardValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The wildcard value such as ALL.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionTable">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the information about a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisiontable.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="collectOperator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the operator that&apos;s used when the result is filtered by the Collect operator.Valid values are: Count Maximum Minimum None Sum</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTable​CollectOperator (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="condition_Criteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Logic that&apos;s used to decide how the input fields are processed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="conditionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Condition logic that&apos;s used for input fields.Valid values are: All Any Custom</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTable​ConditionType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataSource_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the type of data source that&apos;s used to create a decision table.Valid values are: ContextDefinition CsvUpload MultipleSobjects SingleSobject</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTable​DataSourceType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="decisionTable_Parameters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Parameters that you specify in a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableParameter[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="decisionTable_SourceCriterias" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The fields and values from a data source that are used to define the condition logic of the data that&apos;s used in a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableSourceCriteria[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Description of the decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="doesConsider_NullValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a column that has a null value is considered for lookup (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="downloadStatus" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the progress status of a CSV download from a CSV-based lookup table. Available in API version 64.0 and later.Valid values are: Completed DownloadInProgress Failed</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableDownloadStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="executionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the backing storage for the Decision Table. Valid values are: Dmo Hbase Hbpo Solr Soql Execution type of Hbase must be passed in all caps (HBASE) in POST and PATCH calls.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableExecutionType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="filterResultBy" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies how the results of a decision table are filtered if a set of inputs returns multiple matching outputs.Valid values are: AnyValue CollectOperator FirstMatch OutputOrder Priority RuleOrder UniqueValues</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableHitPolicy (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="hasIncremental_SyncFailed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if the last incremental refresh failed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isIncremental_SyncEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if incremental refresh is enabled for the Decision Table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lastIncremental_SyncDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The date and time on which the last incremental refresh occured for the decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lastSyncDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Latest date on which the decision table was refreshed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refresh_FailureReason" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reason why the refresh of the decision table data failed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="refreshStatus" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the refresh status of the cached data in the decision table.Valid values are: Completed Failed InProgress Initiated</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableRefreshStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="setupName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the decision table, which appears in Salesforce Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceCondition_Logic" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The condition logic that&apos;s used to define the decision table from the source data.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Object that contains the rules based on which the decision table must provide outcomes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="status" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Status of the decision table. Valid values are: ActivationInProgress Active Draft Inactive</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Stores the type of decision table.Valid values are: Advanced HighScaleExecution HighVolume LowVolume MediumVolume RealTime</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="uploadStatus" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the progress status of the CSV upload for a CSV based Lookup table.Valid values are: Completed CompletedWithErrors Failed UploadInProgress</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableUploadStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="usageType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of industry or the application within the industry that&apos;s using a decision table.Valid values are: Bre ComplianceControl DecompositionEnrichmentMapping DefaultPricing DefaultRating EventOrchestration FinancialServicesCloud FulfillmentCondition GpaCalculation InsuranceClaimProcessing—Available in API version 65.0 and later. ItServiceManagement—Available in API version 65.0 and later. PlanCostCalculation PriceProtection PricingDiscovery ProductCategoryQualification ProductQualification RatingDiscovery RecordAlert ShipAndDebit StudentInformationSystem—Available in API version 65.0 and later. StudentSuccess TestProcess WarrantyClaim When Business Rules Engine is enabled for a Salesforce instance, the default value is &apos;Bre’. Other usage types are available to you depending on your industry solution and permission sets.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ExpsSetProcessType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionTableDatasetLink">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the information about a dataset link associated with a decision table. In a dataset link, select an object for whose records, the decision table must provide an outcome.This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisiontabledatasetlink.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="decisionTableName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the associated decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="decisionTblDatasetParameters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Mapping between a decision table parameter and a field of the object selected in the dataset link.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTblDatasetParameters</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the dataset link.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isDefault" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a dataset link is the default dataset link for a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="setupName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the decision table dataset link, which appears in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the object being evaluated.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionTableParameter">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an input or output field of a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisiontable.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The data type of the field used in a decision table.Valid values are: Boolean Currency Date DateTime Number Percent String</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DTParameterDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="decimalScale" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The number of digits to the right of the decimal point.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="domainObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For polymorhpic fields, indicates the domain object in the field hierarchy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a field is required to be used for lookups.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="length" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum number of characters supported for a field that&apos;s used in a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Operator used for the input field.Valid values are: Contains DoesNotExistIn DoesNotMatch Equals ExistsIn GreaterOrEqual GreaterThan IsNotNull IsNull LessOrEqual LessThan Matches NotEquals</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableOperator (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The sequence in which input fields are processed. This field is available in API version 52.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Sort outputs of a decision table based on the values of the input or output parameter field. This field is available in API version 56.0 and later.Valid values are: AscNullFirst AscNullLast DescNullFirst DescNullLast None</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableSortType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="usage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Usage type of a field. Valid values are: INPUT OUTPUT ROWCRITERIA</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DecisionTableParameterType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DecisionTableSourceCriteria">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the fields and values from a data source that are used to define the condition logic of the data that&apos;s used in a decision table.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_decisiontable.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The operator that’s applied to an associated decision table’s field to filter the data. Valid values are: Contains DoesNotExistIn DoesNotMatch Equals ExistsIn GreaterOrEqual GreaterThan IsNotNull IsNull LessOrEqual LessThan Matches NotEquals</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DTSourceCriteriaOperator (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequenceNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The sequence number used in the associated decision table&apos;s source condition logic.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The value that’s expected in the source field used in the decision table.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="valueType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of the value that’s used to filter the source data. Valid values are: Formula Literal Lookup Parameter Picklist</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DTSourceCriteriaValueType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DefaultShortcut">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents default keyboard shortcuts assigned to a Salesforce console app. After you enable keyboard shortcuts for a console, several default shortcuts are available for customization. These include opening and closing tabs, moving between tabs, and saving records. Available in API version 28.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="action" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The action performed in the console when a user presses the keyboard shortcut. Valid values are: FOCUS_CONSOLE FOCUS_NAVIGATOR_TAB FOCUS_DETAIL_VIEW FOCUS_PRIMARY_TAB_PANEL FOCUS_SUBTAB_PANEL FOCUS_LIST_VIEW FOCUS_FIRST_LIST_VIEW FOCUS_SEARCH_INPUT MOVE_LEFT MOVE_RIGHT UP_ARROW DOWN_ARROW OPEN_TAB_SCROLLER_MENU OPEN_TAB CLOSE_TAB ENTER EDIT SAVE</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the keyboard shortcut is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyCommand" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The combination of keys a user presses to trigger the keyboard shortcut. Keyboard shortcuts aren’t case-sensitive, but they display as uppercase on setup pages in the Salesforce user interface so that they’re easier to read.Each key command can include up to four modifier keys followed by one non-modifier key. Modifier and non-modifier keys are separated by the + key. Modifier keys can occur in any order, but you must place non-modifier keys at the end of the key command sequence. For example, SHIFT+CTRL+ALT+META +A. Valid modifier keys are: Valid non-modifier keys are letters A through Z and numbers 0 through 9. Other valid keys are:</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DelegateGroup">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a group of users who have the same administrative privileges. These groups are different from public groups used for sharing.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_delegategroup.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="customObjects" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The custom objects associated with the group. Delegated administrators can customize nearly every aspect of each of those custom objects, including creating a custom tab. However, they can’t create or modify relationships on the objects or set organization-wide sharing defaults. Delegated administrators must have access to custom objects to access the merge fields on those objects from formulas.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="groups" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The groups with users assigned by delegated administrators.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The delegated group’s non-API name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="loginAccess" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Allows users in this group to log in as users in the role hierarchy that they administer (true) or not (false). Depending on your organization settings, individual users must grant login access to allow their administrators to log in as them.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="permissionSetGroups" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The permission set groups that can be assigned to users in specified roles and all subordinate roles by delegated administrators.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="permissionSets" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The permission sets that can be assigned to users in specified roles and all subordinate roles by delegated administrators.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="profiles" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The profiles that can be assigned to users by delegated administrators.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="roles" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The roles and subordinates for which delegated administrators of the group can create and edit users.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DgtAssetMgmtProvider">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents external content providers, such as digital asset management (DAM) systems, that integrate with Salesforce CMS. When combined with the DgtAssetMgmtPrvdLghtCpnt type, this metadata type enables organizations to configure external content systems as content providers within the Salesforce platform.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dgtassetmgmtprovider.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="icon" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Stores a reference to the icon resource (typically a Lightning icon or custom image) that visually represents the external content provider in the user interface.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the display label for the external content provider that users see when they select or view the provider.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the primary identifier for the provider in metadata contexts and localization.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DgtAssetMgmtPrvdLghtCpnt">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the Lightning web component configurations for external content providers, such as digital asset management (DAM) systems. This metadata type enables the integration of external content systems with Salesforce CMS using custom Lightning web components.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dgtassetmgmtprvdlghtcpnt.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dgtAssetMgmtProvider" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. References the external content provider, represented by the DgtAssetMgmtProvider type, that this Lightning web component configuration supports.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lightningComponentBundle" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>References the Lightning web component, represented by the LightningComponentBundle type, that implements the user interface for the external content provider in Salesforce CMS. The LightningComponentBundle must be deployed and available before you reference it.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the display name of the Lightning web component configuration as it appears in the UI.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of external content provider Lightning web component that’s being configured. Possible values are: DIGITAL_ASSET_MANAGER: Represents a component that provides full management capabilities for external content providers, including browsing, searching, and selecting. NONE: Represents an undefined or default provider type. Indicates that no specific provider type is assigned.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DgtAssetMgmtPrvdLghtCpntType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DigitalExperience">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents content in the bundle. When retrieved as part of DigitalExperienceBundle, DigitalExperience represents all content for the requested workspace or workspaces. When retrieved on its own, DigitalExperience represents only the content types you specify.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperiencebundle.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="fileName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the resource file.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="filePath" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Path to the file within the artifact folder.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="format" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Only JSON is allowed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DigitalExperienceBundle">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a text-based code structure of your organization’s workspaces, organized by workspace type, and each workspace’s content items.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperiencebundle.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contains the description of the workspace. For site workspaces, this value is empty.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="digitalExperienceFolderShares" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of folders in the source marketing workspace that are shared with target marketing workspaces. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DigitalExperienceFolderShare[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for DigitalExperienceBundle, which is defined when the DigitalExperienceBundle is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="spaceResources" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of resources in this DigitalExperienceBundle. Each resource represents a content type, such as views, routes, themes, and languageSettings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DigitalExperience[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DigitalExperienceConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents details for your organization’s workspaces, such as the site label, site URL path prefix, and workspace type.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperienceconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the site.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="site" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Contains site-related settings, such as the site’s URL path prefix.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Site</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="space" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. References the workspace that contains the site’s content items such as brandingSets, themes, views, and routes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DigitalExperienceFolderShare">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a folder in a source marketing workspace that’s shared with other target marketing workspaces. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperiencebundle.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="folderPath" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The root folder of the shared workspace. The allowed value is _root.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sharedWith" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of target workspaces that the source workspace is shared with.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SharedWith[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DisclosureDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents information that defines a disclosure type, such as details of the publisher or vendor who created or implemented the report.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_disclosuredefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description about the disclosure definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API name of the disclosure type associated with this definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for DisclosureDefinition, which is defined when the DisclosureDefinition is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DisclosureDefinitionVersion">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the version information about the disclosure definition.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_disclosuredefinitionversion.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="authoring_Mode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the authoring mode used to launch the disclosure authoring experience. Possible values are: Microsoft 365 Word Omniscript and Microsoft 365 Word Omniscript Form</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AuthoringMode (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description about the disclosure definition version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureDef_CurrVer" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For internal use only.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API name of the disclosure definition associated with this version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="documentTemplate_GlobalKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The document template global key associated with the DOCX template for the disclosure definition version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the disclosure definition version is an active version (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isCurrentVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether this is the current version of the disclosure definition specified in the disclosureDefinition field (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for DisclosureDefinitionVersion, which is defined when the DisclosureDefinitionVersion is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="omniScriptConfiguration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ID of the Omniscript configuration record.The value of this field is automatically populated using the API name of the OmniScript configuration specified in the omniScriptCnfgApiName field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="versionNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The version of the disclosure definition published by the author.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DisclosureType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the types of disclosures that are done by an individual or an organization and the associated metadata.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_disclosuretype.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description about the disclosure type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureBodyLogo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The logo ID of the standard body to which an individual or a company is making a disclosure.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureBodyUrl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The URL of the disclosure standard body.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disclosureCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the clause category that&apos;s used for disclosure.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for DisclosureType, which is defined when the DisclosureType is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryAIModel">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a model used in Einstein Discovery.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="algorithmType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Algorithm that Einstein Discovery used to create the model associated with this story.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryAlgorithmType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="classificationThreshold" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Threshold value. Applies only to binary classification models. For regression models, this is null.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Model description.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Model label. If you package a model, this label appears in Package Manager.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="modelRuntimeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Model run-time type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryModelRuntimeType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="predictionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of prediction. One of the following strings: Regression Classification Unknown</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryPredictionType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Source type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryModelSourceType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="status" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Model status (enabled or disabled).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryAIModelStatus</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="trainingMetrics" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>JSON object that represents metrics about the model when it was trained.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="transformations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>One or more model transformations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryModelTransform</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryAIModelStatus">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the status of the model (Enabled or Disabled).</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Disabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model is disabled (inactive).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Uploading" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model is uploading.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="UploadFailed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model failed to upload.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="UploadCompleted" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model upload is complete.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Validating" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model is validating.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ValidationFailed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model validation failed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ValidationCompleted" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model validation is complete.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Enabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model is enabled (active).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryAIModelTransformationType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the type of transformation to apply before making a prediction.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="TypographicClustering" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Typographic clustering transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="SentimentAnalysis" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Sentiment analysis transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="FreeTextClustering" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Free text clustering transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="NumericalImputation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Numerical imputation transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="CatagoricalImputation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Catagorical imputation transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="TimeSeriesForecast" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Time series forecast transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ExtractMonthOfYear" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Extract month of year transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ExtractDayOfWeek" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Extract day of week transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ZipCodeAnalysis" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Zip code analysis transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryAlgorithmType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the algorithm that Einstein Discovery used to create the model.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Best" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Tournament Model. Genetic algorithm used to generate high-quality solutions to optimization and search problems, like optimizing decision trees for better performance.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Glm" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Generalized Linear Model. Regression-based algorithm.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Gbm" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Gradient Boost Machine. Decision tree-based ensemble machine learning algorithm.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Xgboost" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>XGBoost. Decision tree-based ensemble machine learning algorithm.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Drf" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Random Forest. Supervised learning algorithm that uses multiple decision trees, randomization, and other optimization techniques.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryCustomPrescribableFieldDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a field definition in custom improvement text.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="filters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents one or more filters associated with custom improvement text.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilter[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="template" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, represents the user-provided template from which the custom text is computed. If not specified, then the default text is used.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryDeployedModel">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a model deployed in Salesforce.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the deployed model is active (True) or inactive (False).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="aiModel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Full name of the DiscoveryAIModel being deployed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="classificationThreshold" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Threshold value. Applies only to binary classification models. For regression models, this is null.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="filters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, one or more segmentation filters for the deployed model. When making a prediction, the first model that has filters matching a specific input row will be used to make the prediction. No filters indicates that the model matches all input rows.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilter[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Label for the deployed model. Appears in Model Manager.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the deployed model.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFieldMap">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a mapping between model variables and field values.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="source" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If the mapping is to a CRM Analytics dataset, this is the name of the dataset. Otherwise, null.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Data source type for field mapping.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFieldMapSourceType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFilter">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a field filter.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Operator used to calculate the filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilterOperator</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of filter value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilterFieldType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="values" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>One or more values selected for the filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilterValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFilterFieldType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the data type of the filter field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Text" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Text field type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Number field type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Date field type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="DateTime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Datetime field type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Boolean" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Boolean field type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFilterOperator">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a filter operator.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Equal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Equal to operator (=).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="NotEqual" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Not equal to operator (&lt;&gt;).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="GreaterThan" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Greater than operator (&gt;).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="GreaterThanOrEqual" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Greater than or equal to operator (&gt;=).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="LessThan" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Less than operator (&lt;).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="LessThanOrEqual" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Less than or equal to operator (&lt;=).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Between" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Between operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="NotBetween" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Not between operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="InSet" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>In set operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="NotIn" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Not in operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Contains" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contains operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="StartsWith" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Starts with operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="EndsWith" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Ends with operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="IsNull" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Is null operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="IsNotNull" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Is not null operator.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFilterValue">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a filter value.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of filter value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilterValueType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilterValue</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryFilterValueType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the type of filter value.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Constant" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Filter value is a constant.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="PlaceHolder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Filter value is a placeholder.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryGoal">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with an Einstein Discovery prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the prediction definition is active (True) or not (False).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="deployedModels" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>One or more deployed models associated with this prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryDeployedModel[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="modelCards" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Model card for this prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryModelCard[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="outcome" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Outcome variable of this prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryGoalOutcome</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="predictionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of prediction: Regression, Classification, or Unknown.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryPredictionType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="pushbackType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of writeback field for predictions.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryPushbackType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subscribedEntity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Salesforce object associated with this model.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="terminalStateFilters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, one or more filter expressions that define the conditions under which an observation has attained its terminal state (the actual outcome has been reached). For performance monitoring, Einstein Discovery determines model accuracy by comparing a model’s predicted outcomes with actual (observed) outcomes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryFilter[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryGoalOutcome">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the outcome variable of the model.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="goal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Goal for the outcome variable.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryOutcomeGoal</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelCard">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a model card associated with an Einstein Discovery prediction definition.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="contactEmail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contact email for this model card.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="contactName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contact name for this model card.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Title for this model card.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sections" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Sections in the model card.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a field (variable) in the model.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isDisparateImpact" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is disparate impact (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isSensitive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is sensitive (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Field label displayed in the UI.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Field name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Field type. Enumerated.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryModelFieldType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="values" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of field values.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelFieldType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the data type of a model field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Text" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Text data type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Number data type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Date" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Date data type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelRuntimeType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the model run-type.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Discovery" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model run-type is Einstein Discovery.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="H2O" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model run-type is H20.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="T" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model run-type is Tensorflow v2.4.4.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Tf27" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model run-type is Tensorflow v2.7.0.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="SC102" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The model run-type is Scikit Learn v1.0.2.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelSourceType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the source tool used to build the model: Discovery or an external tool (the model was uploaded into Salesforce).</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Discovery" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Einstein Discovery built the model.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="UserUpload" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An external tool built the model. The model was then uploaded into Salesforce. This source type is not supported in the Metadata API.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryModelTransform">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a transformation in the model.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoveryaimodel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="config" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The configuration for the transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Type of transformation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryAIModelTransformationType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryOutcomeGoal">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the goal for an outcome.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Minimize" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Maximize the outcome.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Maximize" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Minimize the outcome.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="None" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reserved for future use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryPredictionType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the prediction type for a model.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Unknown" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Unknown prediction type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Regression" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Regression prediction (numeric use case).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Classification" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Binary classification prediction.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="MulticlassClassification" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Multiclass classification prediction.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryPrescribableField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents custom improvement text.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="customDefinitions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>One or more strings for custom improvement text. Uses the default improvement text if none are specified.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryCustomPrescribableFieldDefinition[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the model field that is actionable.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryPushbackType">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the type of writeback field. Must be set to AiRecordInsight.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverygoal.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="AiRecordInsight" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Automatic writeback type. Required.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="Direct" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Currently not supported. Reserved for future use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryStory">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a story used in Einstein Discovery.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverystory.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="application" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The CRM Analytics app the story is associated with.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="autopilot" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The autopilot status for the story. One of the following strings: Enabled Disabled</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryStoryAutopilotStatus</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="classificationThreshold" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The threshold for classification predictions for the story.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The story label. If you package a story, this label appears in Package Manager.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="outcome" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The selected outcome of the story.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryStoryOutcome</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceContainer" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The source ID for the story.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The source type of the story. One of the following strings: AnalyticsDataset LiveDataset Report</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryStorySourceType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="validationContainder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The validation ID for the story.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DiscoveryStoryOutcome">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the selected outcome of the generated story.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_discoverystory.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="failureValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The value if the story failed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="goal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The story outcome goal. One of the following strings: Maximize Minimize None</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryStoryOutcomeGoal</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The story outcome label.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="successValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional. The value if the story succeeded.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The story outcome type. One of the following strings: Categorical Count Number Text</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DiscoveryStoryOutcomeType</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Document">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a Document. All documents must be in a document folder, such as sampleFolder/TestDocument.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_document.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="content" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:base64Binary">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Content of the document. Base 64-encoded binary data. Prior to making an API call, client applications must encode the binary attachment data as base64. Upon receiving a response, client applications must decode the base64 data to binary. This conversion is usually handled for you by a SOAP client. This field is inherited from the MetadataWithContent component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: base64</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the document. Enter a description to distinguish this document from others.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the document, including the folder name. In version 17.0 and earlier, the fullName included the document extension. In version 18.0 and later, the fullName does not include the file extension. The fullName can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters. It must be unique, begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. If this field contained characters before version 14.0 that are no longer allowed, the characters were stripped out of this field, and the previous value of the field was saved in the name field. This field is inherited from the Metadata component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="internalUseOnly" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the document is confidential (true) or not (false). This field and public are mutually exclusive; you cannot set both to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keywords" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Contains one or more words that describe the document. A check for matches to words in this field is performed when doing a search.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of characters allowed in the fullName field has been reduced for versions 14.0 and later. This field contains the value contained in the fullName field before version 14.0. This field is only populated if the value of the fullName field contained characters that are no longer accepted in that field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="public" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the document is an image available for HTML email templates and does not require a Salesforce username and password to view in an email (true) or not (false). If the images will be used as a custom app logo or custom tab icon, both of which require a Salesforce username and password to view, set this field to false. This field and internalUseOnly are mutually exclusive; you cannot set both to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DocumentCategory">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a document category.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_documentcategory.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
