     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableLoyaltyRedeemedPointsExpirationInfoPref" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that automatically calculates and adds the expiration date of points credited back to members for canceled redemptions is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is true. This field is available in API version 55.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableLoyaltyRulesVerifyCdpMemberSegment" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that allows: Loyalty program process rules to process transaction journals only when the loyalty program member is part of a Data Cloud segment associated with the rule&apos;s promotion is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The Promotion Eligibility component on Loyalty Program Member record page to categorize promotions based on whether the member belongs to the promotion’s campaign or Data Cloud segment is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is false. This field is available in API version 55.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableLoyaltyServiceExcellence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Service Console for Loyalty Management is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is false. This field is available in API version 57.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableNegativePointBalance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that lets loyalty program members to hold negative point balances for non-qualifying currencies is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is false. This field is available in API version 61.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableNonQualifyingPointsConsolidation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability to aggregate and expire fixed type non-qualifying points in real time is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is true. This field is available in API version 58.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enablePointsLifecycleTracking" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that allows the company to trace how members redeem their accrued fixed-model non-qualifying points is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is false. This field is available in API version 62.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enablePromSetupProcRuleStatusInheritDplymt" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability, which allows Promotion Setup processes and rules to be deployed to target orgs in the same status as the source orgs when using the LoyaltyProgramSetup metadata type, is enabled (true) or disabled (false). The default value is false. This field is available in API version 62.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableQPRealTimePointBalance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the real time qualifying points balance update capability is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is true. This field is available in API version 55.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableNQPRealTimePointBalance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability to update the non-qualifying point balance of members in real time is enabled (true) or disabled (false) for your org. The default value is true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableSegmentQueryApiMultipleDataSpace" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that allows Query API to verify the Data Cloud segments that customers are part of across multiple data spaces is enabled (true) or not (false). The default value is false. This field is available in API version 64.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableSegmentQueryByDataGraph" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability, which uses Data Cloud data graphs to query for Data Cloud segments that customers are part of, is enabled (true) or disabled (false). The default value is false. This field is available in API version 62.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableTransferPointsToMemberGroupsRealtime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that automates real-time transfer of a member&apos;s non-qualifying points to associated group is enabled (true) or not (false). The default value is false. This field is available in API version 64.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableUsePromPtyUsageForEngmtTrail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the capability that uses Promotion Party Usage records to store attributes for Engagement Trail promotions is enabled (true) or not (false). The default value is true. This field is available in API version 64.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="IndustriesPricingSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the settings for Salesforce Pricing.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_industriespricingsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableDebugPriceLogs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to use price logs to diagnose and resolve pricing issues (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableHighAvailability" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Reserved for internal use.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableHighestPriceCompliance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to track the maximum price of a product over a period of 30 days (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Available in API version 64.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableLowestPriceCompliance" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to track the minimum price of a product over a period of 30 days (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enablePricingProcParallelization" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to run pricing elements in parallel within a pricing procedure to optimize the performance of the pricing execution process (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Available in API version 64.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enablePricingWaterfall" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Price Waterfall (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Price Waterfall provides insights that include price breakups and reasons for every step of the pricing process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enablePricingWaterfallPersistence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Price Waterfall Persistence (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Price Waterfall Persistence stores the process logs that provide insights into the internal pricing processes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableSalesforcePricing" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Salesforce Pricing (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="IndustriesRatingSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the settings for Rate Management.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_industriesratingsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableRating" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Rate Management (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableRatingWaterfall" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Rating Waterfall (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Rating Waterfall provides insights into the rating data, which you can synchronize with your rating lookup tables.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableRatingWaterfallPersistence" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether to enable Rating Waterfall Persistence (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Rating Waterfall Persistence stores rating data, which you can use to enhance the internal processes and increase efficiency.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="IndustriesUnifiedInventorySettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the settings for Industries Unified Inventory.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_industriesunifiedinventorysettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableBatchManagement" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the batch-based inventory management features are enabled (true) or not (false). Within Life Sciences Cloud, this is a core component of the Unified Inventory Extension Entities, supporting Sample Inventory use cases. When enabled, it provides access to the entities ProductionBatch, ProductBatchItem, and InventoryCntProdtBatchItem.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableInventoryCount" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the Inventory Count is enabled (true) or not (false). The Inventory Count provides the ability to manage inventory count processes by planning inventory counts, counting inventory at designated locations, and tracking count results.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableProductInventoryOperations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the Product Inventory Operations that provides the capabilities to perform various actions related to managing product inventory is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Input_Folder">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>The input folder contains a schema.json file with the action inputs. Here’s a sample input schema file.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_genaifunction.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="required" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of all the required properties in the input list.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: array of strings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="properties" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The parent object for all the properties associated with the input.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: object</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lightning_type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Describes the type of input. This value should always be lightning__objectType.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InterestTaggingSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents settings for Interest Tags, which your users can add to client records to capture client needs, interests, and prospecting opportunities.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_interesttaggingsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableInterestTagging" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Enables Interest Tags in your org when set to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InvLatePymntRiskCalcSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the org’s settings to identify the level of risks associated with payment of invoices.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_invlatepymntriskcalcsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableInvLatePymntRiskCalc" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the level of risk associated with payment of an invoice when the value is true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InventorySettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents options for the Salesforce Omnichannel Inventory product.This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_inventorysettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableOCIB2CIntegration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Omnichannel Inventory is allowed to exchange inventory data with B2C Commerce (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableOmniChannelInventory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Omnichannel Inventory features are enabled (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InvocableActionExtension">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the configuration that defines how an action&apos;s inputs are presented in a user interface.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_invocableactionextension.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="targets" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The target of this invocable action extension.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: InvocableActionExtensionTarget[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InvocableActionExtensionTarget">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an extension that can contain attributes for an action&apos;s definition, parameters, and types. Use InvocableActionExtensionTarget as the parent element for a given target, such as an ActionParameter. Each assigned attribute is a child of this element.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_invocableactionextension.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="attributes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of attributes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: InvocableActionExtensionTargetAttribute[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="targetName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the target for the attributes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="targetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of component within the invocable action. Values are: ActionDefinition—Targets the action class. ActionParameter—Targets the specific input/output parameters. TypeDefinition—Targets the custom Apex types used by the action. TypeProperty—Targets the individual properties within those custom types.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: InvocableActionExtTargetType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InvocableActionExtensionTargetAttribute">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the individual configuration attributes within an extension target. Use InvocableActionExtensionTargetAttribute as the child element of InvocableActionExtensionTarget to define specific behaviors, dependencies, and properties. Each attribute consists of a key-value pair with an associated data type. This configuration determines how the target action parameter, type property, or action definition behaves.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_invocableactionextension.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The data type of the value stored in the value field. Values are: Boolean Date Double Integer Long String</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: InvocableActionExtAttributeDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="key" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The key field that specifies which standard attribute to provide a value for, or provides a custom key. The available standard keys are: Order GroupName ControllingField For a custom key, enter any value that contains letters, numbers, or single underscores, starts with a letter, and ends with __c.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of the associated key. An Invocable Action Extension can have multiple attributes, each with its own value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="InvocableActionSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the org’s invocable action settings, such as whether partial save is allowed.This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_invocableactionsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isPartialSaveAllowed" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether partial save is enabled for most invocable actions that are invoked via REST API and executed in bulk. When the value is true, Salesforce tries three times to execute invocable actions that run successfully and rolls back only the invocable actions that fail to execute. This functionality is called partial save. If the field is set to false, if one invocable action fails, Salesforce rolls back other invocable actions in the same transaction and the entire transaction fails.Corresponds to the Enable Partial Save for Invocable Actions critical update.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KeyboardShortcuts">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents keyboard shortcuts assigned to a Salesforce console app. Required if isServiceCloudConsole is true. Available in API version 28.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="customShortcuts" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents custom keyboard shortcuts assigned to a Salesforce console app in Salesforce Classic. Before you can create custom shortcuts, a developer must define the shortcut’s action with the addEventListener() method in the Salesforce Console Integration Toolkit. You can’t create keyboard shortcuts for actions performed outside of the console.In API version 42.0, this field was renamed from customShortcut to customShortcuts.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomShortcut[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultShortcuts" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents default keyboard shortcuts assigned to a Salesforce console app. After you enable keyboard shortcuts for a console, several default shortcuts are available for customization. These include opening and closing tabs, moving between tabs, and saving records.In API version 42.0, this field was renamed from defaultShortcut to defaultShortcuts.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DefaultShortcut[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Keyword">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Keywords in the keyword list.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_keywordlist.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="keyword" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Keywords you want to moderate. Keywords can only be up to 100 characters and can include letters, numbers, spaces, and special characters. Wildcard characters aren’t supported.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KeywordList">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a list of keywords used in Experience Cloud site moderation. This keyword list is a type of moderation criteria that defines offensive language or inappropriate content that you don’t want in your site.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_keywordlist.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="Description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the keyword list.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keywords" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The keywords you want moderate in your Experience Cloud site.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Keyword[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Label for the keyword list.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeAnswerSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Answers.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="assignTo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the username an article is assigned to from Answers.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultArticleType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default article type for articles created from Answers. Uses the API name of the article type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableArticleCreation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether users can create articles from Answers (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeCaseField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the name of the case field used to suggest articles for the case. Available in API version 37.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the name of the case field used to suggest articles for the case.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeCaseSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Cases.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="articlePDFCreationProfile" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The profile used to create a PDF of an article from Cases.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="articlePublicSharingSites" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Sites.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeSitesSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="articlePublicSharingCommunities" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Experience Cloud sites.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeSitesSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="articlePublicSharingSitesChatterAnswers" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Sites with Chatter Answers.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeSitesSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="assignTo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the username an article is assigned to from Cases.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customizationClass" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the Apex class used for customization.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultContributionArticleType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default article type for articles created from Cases.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="editor" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the rich text editor type. Valid values are: simple standard</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeCaseEditor (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableArticleCreation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether users can create articles from Cases (true) or not (false). Controls whether other fields on KnowledgeCaseSettings can be set.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableArticlePublicSharingSites" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether articles can be shared via a public site (URL) from Cases (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableCaseDataCategoryMapping" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Case Data Category mapping is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="useProfileForPDFCreation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a profile is used to create a PDF of an article from Cases (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeLanguage">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for the languages enabled for Salesforce Knowledge. KnowledgeLanguage is available in API version 28.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the language is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultAssignee" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default assignee for articles in the language.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultAssigneeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the default assignee type. Valid values are: User Queue</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeLanguageLookupValueType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultReviewer" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default reviewer for articles in the language.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultReviewerType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the default reviewer type. Valid values are: User Queue</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeLanguageLookupValueType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The code for the language name, for example: English is en. See “What languages does Salesforce support?” in the Salesforce Help for a list of supported languages and their codes.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeLanguageSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A list of languages enabled for Salesforce Knowledge. KnowledgeLanguageSettings is available in API version 28.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="language" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for the languages enabled for Salesforce Knowledge.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeLanguage[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_knowledgesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="answers" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Answers.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeAnswerSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="cases" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for Salesforce Knowledge and Cases.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeCaseSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultLanguage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The default language for Salesforce Knowledge. Use the abbreviation for the language, for example, en_US for United States English.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableChatterQuestionKBDeflection" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether tracking for case deflection via Chatter is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableCreateEditOnArticlesTab" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether users can create and edit articles on the articles tab (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableExternalMediaContent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether connecting to external media is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKbStandardSharing" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether standard Salesforce sharing is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledge" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Salesforce Knowledge is enabled (true) or not (false). This field is false by default.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeAgentContribution" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a user can create an article from a case (true) or not (false). (Classic only)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeArticleTextHighlights" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether text snippet highlights in Salesforce Knowledge search results are enabled (true) or not (false). This field is true by default. Available in API version 47.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeAnswersPromotion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a user can create an article from a reply (true) or not (false). (Classic Only)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeCaseRL" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether creating a list of cases linked to an article is enabled (true) or not (false). (Classic Only)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeKeywordAutoComplete" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether auto-complete for keywords is enabled (true) or not (false) when searching Salesforce Knowledge. This field is true by default. Available in API version 47.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableKnowledgeTitleAutoComplete" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether auto-complete for article titles is enabled (true) or not (false) when searching Salesforce Knowledge. This field is true by default. Available in API version 47.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableLightningKnowledge" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether Lightning Knowledge is enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="languages" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of languages enabled for Salesforce Knowledge.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeLanguageSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="showArticleSummariesCustomerPortal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether article summaries appear in the Customer Portal (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="showArticleSummariesInternalApp" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether article summaries appear in the internal knowledge base (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="showArticleSummariesPartnerPortal" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether article summaries appear in the partner portal (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="suggestedArticles" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata used to manage settings for the case fields used to suggest articles for cases. Available in API version 37.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KnowledgeSuggestedArticlesSettings</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="votingEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>When true, enables users to vote for a product or feature that uses Vote, such as Articles in Knowledge. Available in API version 50.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="KnowledgeSitesSettings">
