 <xsd:complexType name="ReputationPointsRule">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the event and associated point value for a points rule. When a user acts, they accrue the associated points.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_network.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="eventType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of event a member has to perform to get points. The available values are: FeedItemWriteAPost FeedItemWriteAComment FeedItemReceiveAComment FeedItemLikeSomething FeedItemReceiveALike FeedItemMentionSomeone FeedItemSomeoneMentionsYou FeedItemShareAPost FeedItemSomeoneSharesYourPost FeedItemPostAQuestion FeedItemAnswerAQuestion FeedItemReceiveAnAnswer FeedItemMarkAnswerAsBest FeedItemYourAnswerMarkedBest FeedItemEndorseSomeoneForKnowledgeOnATopic FeedItemEndorsedForKnowledgeOnATopic</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="points" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The number of points a member gets for performing the event. The default number of points per event is: FeedItemWriteAPost +1 FeedItemWriteAComment: +1 FeedItemReceiveAComment: +5 FeedItemLikeSomething: +1 FeedItemReceiveALike: +5 FeedItemMentionSomeone: +1 FeedItemSomeoneMentionsYou: +5 FeedItemShareAPost: +1 FeedItemSomeoneSharesYourPost: +5 FeedItemPostAQuestion: +1 FeedItemAnswerAQuestion: +5 FeedItemReceiveAnAnswer: +5 FeedItemMarkAnswerAsBest: +5 FeedItemYourAnswerMarkedBest: +20 FeedItemEndorseSomeoneForKnowledgeOnATopic: +5 FeedItemEndorsedForKnowledgeOnATopic: +20</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ReputationPointsRules">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents points rules in an Experience Cloud site’s point system.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_network.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="pointsRule" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents events and their associated points.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ReputationPointsRule[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="RuleEntry">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the fields used by the rule.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_escalationrules.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="booleanFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Advanced filter conditions that were specified for the rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="businessHours" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The hours when escalation actions are performed. Specify only if businessHoursSource is set to Static.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="businessHoursSource" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Valid values are: None Case Static</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: BusinessHoursSourceType (enumerations of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="criteriaItems" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The items in the list that define the assignment criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FilterItem</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="disableEscalationWhenModified" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the escalation is disabled when the record is modified true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="escalationAction" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The actions to perform when the escalation criteria are met.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: EscalationAction[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="escalationStartTime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the start time for the escalation. Valid values are: CaseCreation CaseLastModified</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: EscalationStartTimeType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="formula" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The validation formula. Specify either formula or criteriaItems, but not both fields.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ScheduledRecommendation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a list of scheduled recommendations. Available in API version 41.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_network.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="scheduledRecommendationDetails" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of scheduled recommendations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ScheduledRecommendationDetail[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ScheduledRecommendationDetail">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>The specific details of a scheduled recommendation. Available in API version 41.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_network.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="channel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A way to group recommendations together to determine where they show up in the site. The valid values are: DefaultChannel—The default recommendation channel. Recommendations in the default channel appear in predefined locations, such as directly in the feed in Salesforce mobile web and on the Home and Question Detail pages of the Customer Service (Napili) template. CustomChannel1—A custom recommendation channel. Choose where you want recommendations to appear by adding the Recommendations Carousel component to the page in Experience Builder. CustomChannel2—A custom recommendation channel. CustomChannel3—A custom recommendation channel. CustomChannel4—A custom recommendation channel. CustomChannel5—A custom recommendation channel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: RecommendationChannel (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether scheduling is enabled. If true, the recommendation is enabled and appears in sites.If false, recommendations in feeds in Salesforce mobile web aren’t removed, but no new recommendations appear. In sites, disabled recommendations no longer appear.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rank" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The rank of the recommendation within the channel, which determines the order in which it’s displayed.The scheduled recommendation is inserted into the position specified by the rank. The rank of all the scheduled recommendations after it is pushed down. If the specified rank is larger than the size of the list, the scheduled recommendation is put at the end of the list. If a rank isn’t specified, the scheduled recommendation is put at the end of the list.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="recommendationAudience" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the audience for this scheduled recommendation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Scontrol">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Deprecated. Represents an Scontrol component, corresponding to an s-control in the Salesforce user interface.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_scontrol.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="content" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:base64Binary">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Content of the s-control. Base 64-encoded binary data. Before making an API call, client applications must encode the binary attachment data as base64. Upon receiving a response, client applications must decode the base64 data to binary. This conversion is handled for you by a SOAP client. This field is inherited from the MetadataWithContent component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: base64Binary</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="contentSource" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Determines how you plan to use the s-control: HTML: Select this option if you want to enter the content for your s-control in content. URL: Select this option if you want to enter the link or URL of an external website in content. Snippet: Snippets are s-controls that are designed to be included in other s-controls. Select this option if you want to enter the content for your s-control snippet in content.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SControlContentSource (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Optional text that describes the s-control. This only displays to users with View All Data permission (administrator).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="encodingKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The default encoding setting is Unicode: UTF-8. Change it if you’re passing information to a URL that requires data in a different format. This option is available when you select URL as the value for contentSource.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Encoding (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fileContent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:base64Binary">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>File contents displayed if you add this s-control to a custom link. The file can contain a Java applet, Active-X control, or any other type of content you want. This option only applies to s-controls with a value of HTML for contentSource.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: base64</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fileName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The unique name for the s-control. This name can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters, and must be unique in your org. It must begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. This field can’t be changed for components installed by a managed package. It’s only relevant if the fileContent field also has a value. This field is available in API version 14.0.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The s-control developer name used as a unique identifier for API access. The fullName can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters. It must be unique, begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. If this field contained characters before version 14.0 that are no longer allowed, the characters were stripped out of this field, and the previous value of the field was saved in the name field. This field is inherited from the Metadata component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The unique name for the s-control. It must contain alphanumeric characters only and begin with a letter. For example example_s_control.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportsCaching" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the s-control supports caching (true) or not (false). Caching optimizes the page so that it remembers which s-controls are on the page when it reloads. This option only applies to HTML s-controls.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ScontrolTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The translated s-control name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the s-control.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SearchCustomization">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the configuration of search settings created in Search Manager. The configuration includes the search channel, searchable objects and fields, and rules to filter search results.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_searchcustomization.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="channel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The search channel that the configuration applies to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the configuration.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectOverride" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of object configurations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SearchCustomizationObjectOverride[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectToAlwaysSearch" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of the objects that are always searched for the user profile if the search channel is Einstein Global Search Bar.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="profile" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies user profile if the search channel is Einstein Global Search Bar.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="selectedObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of the objects that are selected in the configuration if the search channel is LWR Experience Sites.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="selectedProfile" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies all user profiles that are associated with a Search configuration if the search channel is Einstein Global Search Bar. This field is available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SearchCustomizationFieldOverride">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the configuration for a specific field within an object.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_searchcustomization.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="searchable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the field is searchable (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SearchCustomizationObjectOverride">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the configuration for a specific object.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_searchcustomization.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="objectApiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API name of the object that the configuration is applied to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rule" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of rules applied to filter search results.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SearchCustomizationRule[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="searchable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the object is searchable (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SearchCustomizationRule">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the rules defined in an object to filter search results.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_searchcustomization.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The operator for the rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ruleValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of rule values.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SearchCustomizationRuleValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SearchCustomizationRuleValue">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the value of a rule used to filter search results.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_searchcustomization.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="targetObjectApiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The API name of the target object, in case the rule applies to a lookup field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of the rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceAISetupDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents settings for an Einstein for Service feature such as Einstein Article Recommendations. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceAIsetupdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="appSourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The target application for the configuration. Valid values are: REPLY_RECOMMENDATION—Einstein Reply Recommendations ARTICLE_RECOMMENDATION—Einstein Article Recommendations UTTERANCE_RECOMMENDATION—Einstein Bot utterances FAQ—Einstein Bot frequently asked questions</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ApplicationSourceType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A reference to the configuration.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="setupStatus" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The status of the configuration. Valid values are: FIELDS_SELECTED TRAINING READY_TO_ACTIVATE SERVING RETIRED ARCHIVED READY_FOR_REVIEW</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceAISetupDefStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportedLanguages" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required when appSourceType is ARTICLE_RECOMMENDATION. Language codes for selected and supported languages.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceAISetupField">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a field on cases or knowledge articles that Einstein uses to identify relevant articles in Einstein Article Recommendations. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceAIsetupfield.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="entity" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The Case or KnowledgeArticle object for the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A reference to the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="setupDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A reference to the parent ServiceAISetupDefinition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceChannel">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a channel of work items that are received from your organization—for example, cases, chats, or leads.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_servicechannel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="acwExtensionDuration" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum length of time, measured in seconds, an agent can spend on After Conversation Work (ACW) each time they extend the timer. You must set this field if hasAcwExtensionEnabled is set to true. Specify a value from 10 through 3600. Available only for service channels of type Messaging or Voice.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="afterConvoMaxTime" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum length of time, measured in seconds, an agent has to complete After Conversation Work (ACW). You must set this field if hasAfterConvoWorkTimer is set to true. Specify a value from 10 through 3600. Available only for service channels of type Messaging or Voice.For service channels of type Voice, this field is available in API version 52.0 and later. For service channels of type Messaging, this field is available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="capacityModel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The method that determines when an agent&apos;s capacity for a work item is released. With the status-based capacity routing model, work remains assigned and applied to an agent’s capacity until the work is completed or reassigned to a different agent. In contrast, the tab-based capacity routing model releases an agent’s capacity when a work tab is closed in the service console. This field is available in API version 65.0 and later.Values are: STATUS_BASED TAB_BASED</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="doesCheckCapOnOwnerChange" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the override for capacity check is on (true) or not (false). If it is on, when work is reassigned to another agent it overrides it and keeps the work assigned to the specific agent. The default value is false.This field is available in API version 65.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="doesCheckCapOnStatusChange" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the override for capacity check is on (true) or not (false). If it is on, when work is reopened it is re-assigned to a specific agent. The default value is false. This field is available in API version 65.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="doesMinimizeWidgetOnAccept" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Automatically minimizes the Omni-Channel widget when an agent accepts work. This field is available in API version 48.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="hasAcwExtensionEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, agents can extend their After Conversation Work (ACW) time. Available only if hasAfterConvoWorkTimer is set to true. If set to true, you must also set the acwExtensionDuration and maxExtensions fields. The default value is false. Available only for service channels of type Messaging or Voice. This field is available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="hasAfterConvoWorkTimer" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If set to true, After Conversation Work (ACW) time can be configured for the channel. If set to true, you must also set the afterConvoWorkMaxTime field. The default value is false. Available only for service channels of type Messaging or Voice.For service channels of type Voice, this field is available in API version 52.0 and later. For service channels of type messaging, this field is available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="hasAutoAcceptEnabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Work items in a service channel open automatically in the agent’s workspace so that the agent doesn’t have to manually accept them.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="interactionComponent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The custom console component to open in the footer when an agent accepts a work item from this service channel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isInterruptible" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether a work item consumes interruptible or primary capacity. The default value is false. Available in API version 57.0 and later when the Interruptible Capacity feature is enabled.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The label of the service channel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="maxExtensions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum number of times an agent can extend their After Work Conversation (ACW) time. Specify a value from 1 through 10. You must set this field if hasAcwExtensionEnabled is set to true. Available only for service channels of type Messaging or Voice. This field is available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relatedEntityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of object that’s associated with this service channel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceChannelFieldPriority">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a secondary routing priority field value mapping. Available in API version 47.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_servicechannel.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="priority" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The priority number assigned to the mapped field value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The work item status assigned to the mapped field value. Possible types are IN_PROGRESS, PAUSED, COMPLETED.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: picklist</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of Status Field defined in the parent ServiceChannel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of the secondaryRoutingPriorityField field defined in the parent ServiceChannel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceChannelStatus">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the status that’s associated with a specific service channel.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_servicepresencestatus.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="channel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the channels assigned to the presence status.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceCloudConsoleConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents configuration settings for a Salesforce console app. Available in API version 42.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="componentList" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents custom console components (Visualforce pages) assigned to a Salesforce console app.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: AppComponentList</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="detailPageRefreshMethod" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines how detail pages refresh in a Salesforce console app. Required if isServiceCloudConsole is true. The valid values are: none autoRefresh flag</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="footerColor" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines the footer color in a Salesforce console app. Specify the color with a hexadecimal code, such as #0000FF for blue.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="headerColor" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines the header color in a Salesforce console app. Specify the color with a hexadecimal code, such as #0000FF for blue.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyboardShortcuts" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the keyboard shortcuts for a Salesforce console app. Keyboard shortcuts let users perform actions by pressing a combination of keys instead of having to use a mouse.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: KeyboardShortcuts</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="listPlacement" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents how lists display in a Salesforce console app. Required if isServiceCloudConsole is true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ListPlacement</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="listRefreshMethod" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines how lists refresh in a Salesforce console app. Required if isServiceCloudConsole is true. The valid values are: none refreshList refreshListRows</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="liveAgentConfig" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the configurations for using Chat in the Salesforce Console.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: LiveAgentConfig</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="primaryTabColor" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines the primary tab color in a Salesforce console app. Specify the color with a hexadecimal code, such as #0000FF for blue.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="pushNotifications" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents push notifications for a Salesforce console app. Push notifications are visual indicators on lists and detail pages that show when a record or field has changed during a user’s session. For example, assume that two support agents are working on the same case. If one agent changes the Priority, a push notification displays to the other agent so the agent notices the change and doesn’t duplicate the effort.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: PushNotification[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="tabLimitConfig" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the maximum number of primary tabs and subtabs allowed in one Salesforce console session. Required if enableTabLimits is true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TabLimitConfig</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="whiteListedDomains" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Any external domains that users can access from within a Salesforce console app. For example, www.yourdomain.com.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServicePresenceStatus">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a presence status that can be assigned to a service channel. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_servicepresencestatus.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="channels" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the status that’s associated with a specific service channel.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceChannelStatus</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The label of the presence status.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceProcess">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a process created in Service Process Studio and its associated attributes.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceprocess.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A meaningful explanation of the service process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="processLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A meaningful name for the service process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="serviceProcessAttributes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Custom attributes that store the data associated with the service process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceProcessAttribute[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="serviceProcessDependencies" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Dependent components of the service process, such as OmniScripts or flows.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceProcessDependency[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="serviceProcessItemGroups" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Groups of related ServiceProcessAttribute records.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ServiceProcessItemGroup[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="shortDescription" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A brief meaningful explanation of the service process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="usageType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The Cloud that uses this service process. Values are: CustomerService Employee FinancialServices Industry (available in version 58.0 and later)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemUsageType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceProcessAttribute">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A custom attribute that stores data associated with a service process. For example, a service process that reverses a fee can have a Fee Type attribute.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceprocess.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="attributeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A Base attribute corresponds to a SvcCatalogRequest field, which is subject to field-level security. An Extended attribute is only a ServiceProcessAttribute object record, which isn&apos;t subject to field-level security.Values are: Base Extended The default is Extended.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCtlgItemAttrAttributeType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The data type of the attribute.Values are: Checkbox Currency Date Datetime Integer ListOfBoolean ListOfDouble ListOfInteger ListOfMaps ListOfString Map Number Percentage Text The default is Text. Selecting Currency doesn&apos;t cause an error, but currency conversions aren&apos;t supported.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemAttrDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A meaningful explanation of the attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A system name for the attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="groupApiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The apiName of the ServiceProcessItemGroup to which this attribute belongs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inputVariableValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default value of the attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether the attribute is required. The default is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A meaningful name for the attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parentAttribute" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The parent attribute of this attribute. For example, a Latitude attribute can have GeoLocation as a parent.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The position of the attribute in the payload relative to other attributes having no parent or the same parent.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceProcessDependency">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A dependent component of the service process, which can be a flow, an OmniScript, an Integration Definition, or a preprocessor Apex class.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceprocess.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="dependencyReference" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The Developer Name of the flow, OmniScript, Integration Definition, or preprocessor Apex class.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="processStepName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the step in a service process.Values are: FulfillmentFlow IntegrationDefinition Preprocessor RequestForm</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCtlgItemDpndProcType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of dependent component.Values are: FlowDefinition IntegrationProviderDef OmniScriptConfig PreprocessorApexClass</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemDependencyType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ServiceProcessItemGroup">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A group of related ServiceProcessAttribute records.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_serviceprocess.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="apiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API Name of the group.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="groupName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the group.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The group display order.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SharedWith">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a target marketing workspace that the source marketing workspace is shared with. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperiencebundle.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="fullyQualifiedName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The target workspace that the source workspace is shared with. It uses the format workspace_type/target_workspace_name. For example, marketing/Workspace2.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Site">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents site-related information, such as the URL path prefix.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_digitalexperienceconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="urlPathPrefix" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The first part of the path on the site&apos;s URL that distinguishes this site from other sites. For example, if your site URL is MyDomainName.my.site.com/partners, then partners is the urlPathPrefix.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SiteDotCom">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a site for deployment.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_sitedotcom.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the site that you’re deploying.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="siteType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Identifies whether the site is a ChatterNetworkPicasso site for Experience Cloud Sites, or a Siteforce site for Site.com sites.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Skill">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the settings for a skill used for field service or to route chats to agents in Chat, such as the name of the skill and which agents the skills are assigned to.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_skills.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="assignments" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies how skills are assigned to Chat users. Skills can be assigned to sets of users or sets of profiles.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SkillAssignments</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the description of the skill. This field is available in API version 38.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the name of the skill.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="skillType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the skill type, such as language or department, associated with the skill. This field is available in API version 58.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageAssignment">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to automatically assign stage definitions to records based on rule criteria.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stageassignment.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the stage assignment rule is active (true) or not (false). The default value is true. Active rules are evaluated when determining stage definition assignments.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Description for the stage assignment rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for the stage assignment rule, which is defined when the metadata component is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="referenceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Reference object that&apos;s associated with the stage assignment rule. This is the API name of the Salesforce object for which the stage assignment rule applies (for example, ApplicationForm or Order).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="referenceObjectRecordType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Record type of a reference object that&apos;s associated with the stage assignment rule. When specified, the assignment rule applies only to records of the specified record type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ruleCriteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Collection of rule criteria to determine stage definition assignment. Rules are evaluated in priority order, and the first matching rule determines which stage definition is assigned to the record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgAssignmentRuleCriteria[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stageDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Default stage definition to assign when no rule criteria match. This provides a fallback assignment when none of the defined rule criteria evaluate to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageCondition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the rules in transition criteria and stage change, including the object state, logic, and values.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the operator used in the transition criteria. Values are: Contains DoesNotContain Equals GreaterOrEqual GreaterThan LessOrEqual LessThan NotEqualTo StartsWith</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageConditionOperator (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequenceNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the order of the object state transition condition in a sequence.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Value of the field used in the transition criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageCriteria">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the criteria for the object stage transition and object stage change.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="condition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the rules in transition criteria and stage change, including the object state, logic, and values.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCondition[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="criteriaType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the criteria type used to execute the transition. Values are: AND CUSTOMLOGIC OR</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCriteriaType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="errorMessage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A custom error message that&apos;s displayed when stage transition criteria evaluation fails. Available in API version 64.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="executionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of logic used to execute the criteria. Values are: CONDITION FLOW</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCriteriaExecType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flowDefinitionName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the developer name of the Flow that executes when the criteria execution type is set to FLOW. Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isChildObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the target object in the stage criteria represents a child object in a parent-child relationship (true) or not (false).Available in API version 63.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="logicalExpression" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Formula to specify custom logic. Compares the Criteria field to the Value field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="targetObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Object that&apos;s used in a Parent-Child object relationship condition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the states and transitions for Stage Management.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the stage definition is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the stage definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for stage definition, which is defined when the metadata component is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="referenceObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The reference object associated with the stage definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="referenceObjectRecordType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The record type of a reference object associated with the stage definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stageTransition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up transitions between two states.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageTransition[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stageValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the field values of an object for which stages are defined.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageTransition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up transitions between two states.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="criteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the criteria for the object stage transition and object stage change.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCriteria[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customPermission" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The custom permission associated with the stage transition. The custom permission required to initiate a stage change.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fromStageValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The From Stage that&apos;s associated with the referenced object&apos;s stage transition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stepGroup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgFulfillmentStepDefGrp[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="toStageValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The To Stagethat&apos;s associated with the referenced object&apos;s stage transition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userPermission" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the type of user permission needed to initiate a stage change.Values are: CoordinateClinicalTrials CoordinateClnclTrialExprcUsr ManageClinicalTrials ParticipateClinicalTrials ProcessOrder</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageUserPermission (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StageValue">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the field values of an object for which stages are defined.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="criteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the criteria for the object stage transition and object stage change.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCriteria[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stepGroup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgFulfillmentStepDefGrp[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of the field used in the transition criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StandardValueSet">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the set of values in a standard picklist field. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_standardvalueset.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="groupingStringEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Groups picklist and enumerated values. For example, for the picklist values of the Status field on the Service Appointment object, Done and Finished can both have a grouping string of Completed. Available in API version 41.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sorted" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether a global value set is sorted in alphabetical order. By default, this value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="standardValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Defines each value in a standard picklist’s value set. The groupingString value is available in API version 38.0 and later. When you deploy a StandardValueSet, this array must contain at least one picklist value. Otherwise, you receive an error. When setting standardValue on Record Types, including person account record types, new picklist values loaded into your organization through the Metadata API don’t display in the picklist UI by default. For users to see the new values, go to the Record Types list for the object containing the picklist field, click Edit, and add the new value to the Selected Fields list.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StandardValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StandardValueSetTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Contains details for a standard picklist translation. It returns a translated standard value set.This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_standardvaluesettranslation.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="valueTranslation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of values from global value sets to be translated.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ValueTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="State">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>This metadata type provides the definition for a state in a picklist.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_addresssettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines whether the value is available in the API.After you enable state and country/territory picklists in your Salesforce organization, you can’t set the active status to false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="integrationValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A customizable text value that is linked to a state or country/territory code. Integration values for standard states, countries, and territories default to the full ISO-standard state, country, and territory names. Integration values function similarly to the API names of custom fields and objects. Configuring integration values allows integrations that you set up before enabling state and country/territory picklists to continue to work.If you don’t specify integration values before enabling state and country/territory picklists in your organization, records use the default value provided by Salesforce. If you change integration values later, records created or updated from that point on use your edited values.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isoCode" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ISO-standard code populates this field when you issue a retrieve() call. This field is read only in the API but you can edit the label in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The label is what users see in picklists in Salesforce. This field is read only in the API but you can edit the label in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="standard" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Standard states and countries are states and countries that are included with Salesforce. You can’t edit the standard attribute.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="visible" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Makes the state, country, or territory available to users in Salesforce. States, countries, or territories that are visible must also be active.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StaticResource">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a static resource file, often a code library in a ZIP file. Static resources allow you to upload content that you can reference in a Visualforce page, including archives (such as .zip and .jar files), images, style sheets, JavaScript, and other files. Static resources can be used only within your Salesforce org, so you can’t host content here for other apps or websites.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_staticresource.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="cacheControl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the static resource is marked with a public caching tag so that a third-party delivery client can cache the content. This field is available in API version 14.0. The valid values are: Private Public</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StaticResourceCacheControl (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="content" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:base64Binary">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The static resource content. Base 64-encoded binary data. Before making an API call, client applications must encode the binary attachment data as base64. Upon receiving a response, client applications must decode the base64 data to binary. This conversion is handled for you by a SOAP client. This field is inherited from the MetadataWithContent component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: base64Binary</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="contentType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The content type of the file, for example text/plain.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the static resource.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The static resource name. The name can only contain characters, letters, and the underscore (_) character. The name must start with a letter, and can’t end with an underscore or contain two consecutive underscore characters. Inherited from the Metadata component, this field isn’t defined in the WSDL for this component. It must be specified when creating, updating, or deleting. See create() to see an example of this field specified for a call.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StgAssignmentRuleCond">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to define individual condition rules for stage assignment rule criteria. Each condition compares a field value against a specified value using a comparison operator.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stageassignment.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Operator that&apos;s used to evaluate the field value. Valid values are: Contains DoesNotContain Equals GreaterOrEqual GreaterThan LessOrEqual LessThan NotEqualTo StartsWith</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageConditionOperator (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequenceNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the sequence number of this condition for reference in logical expressions. The sequence number is used in the logicalExpression field to create custom boolean logic. For example, a condition with sequenceNumber 1 is referenced as &quot;1&quot; in the expression &quot;1 AND 2&quot;.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Defines the value to compare against the field value. The value is specified as a string regardless of the field type. For example, numeric values are specified as &quot;10000&quot;, dates as &quot;2025-10-27&quot;, and text values as &quot;Approved&quot;.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StgAssignmentRuleCriteria">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to define rule criteria for stage definition assignment. Rule criteria are evaluated in priority order, with lower priority numbers evaluated first.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stageassignment.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="condition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Collection of conditions to evaluate for this rule criteria. You can combine multiple conditions by using the criteriaType field to determine the overall evaluation result.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgAssignmentRuleCond[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="criteriaType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the criteria type that&apos;s used to evaluate the rule conditions. Valid values are: AND CUSTOMLOGIC OR</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StageCriteriaType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="logicalExpression" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Formula to specify custom logic for evaluating conditions. It&apos;s used when criteriaType is set to CUSTOMLOGIC.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the rule criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="priority" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Priority order for evaluating this rule criteria when multiple criteria are defined. Rules are evaluated in ascending priority order where lower numbers have higher priority. For example, a rule with priority 1 is evaluated before a rule with priority 2. The first rule that evaluates to true determines the stage definition assignment.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stageDefinition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Stage definition to assign when this rule criteria matches. This must be the API name of a valid StageDefinition for the same reference object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StgFulfillmentStepDef">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up fullfillment step definitions for stages and transitions.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="apiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The developer name of the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="assignedToQueue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The queue associated with the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="assignedToUser" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The user associated with the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dependency" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up the stage fulfillment step dependency between two steps.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgFulfillmentStepDpndDef[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="executeOnRule" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the expression set for the fulfillment step. The step is executed only when the corresponding expression set is set to true. Available in API version 62.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flowDefinitionName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the flow added to the step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="integrationDefinitionName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ID associated with the integration provider definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="omniscriptName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the Omniscript defined in step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="runAsUser" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ID of the user associated with the step definition. The user required to execute the step definition.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="stepType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of fulfillment step.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StgFulfillmentStepDefGrp">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the stage fulfillment step definition.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the stage fulfillment step definition group.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="step" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields to set up fullfillment step definitions for stages and transitions.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StgFulfillmentStepDef[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StgFulfillmentStepDpndDef">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a collection of fields to set up the stage fulfillment step dependency between two steps.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_stagedefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="step" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The step definition for the fulfillment step.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="StreamingAppDataConnector">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the connection information specific to Web and Mobile Connectors.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_streamingappdataconnector.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="appIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The unique app identifier (UUID).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataConnectorType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The value of the field is restricted to SteamingApp.Possible values are: DataCloud StreamingApp</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The display name of the connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="streamingAppDataConnectorType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of connector.Possible values are: MobileApp WebApp</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: StreamingAppDataConnectorType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SustainabilityUom">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the unit of measure (UOM) values for custom fuel types in an org. Track fuel consumption and emission results with the flexibility to add custom fuel types and UOM values.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_sustainabilityuom.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the unit of measure.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProductUom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the unit of measure is for a product that the company has procured in its supply chain operations (true) or not (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isStationaryAssetUom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the unit of measure is used in the stationary asset calculations (true) or (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isVehicleAssetUom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the unit of measure is used in the vehicle asset calculations (true) or (false). The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The label assigned to this object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="unitType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of unit used for conversions or calculations. Values are: Energy Other Volume Weight</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UnitType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SustnUomConversion">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents information about the unit of measure (UOM) conversion for the custom fuel types defined by a customer in an org.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_sustnuomconversion.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="conversionFactor" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The conversion factor that&apos;s used to convert values from one unit of measure to another for the fuel type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fuelType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the fuel type.Possible values are: AutogasLPG Biodiesel Biomass CityGas CompressedNaturalGasCNG Cooling Diesel Electricity Ethanol FuelOil Gasoline Heat HeavyOil ITElectricity JetFuel Kerosene LightOil LiquidNaturalGasLNG MobileDiesel NaturalGas Propane Refrigerant Steam</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A user-friendly name for SustnUomConversion, which is defined when the SustnUomConversion is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sourceUom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The source unit of measure for the fuel type. Possible values are: 1000m3 GJ GWh Kiloliters Liters MJ MMBtu MWh Therms Tonnes UkGallons UsGallons ccf kG kWh kcal lbs longTons m3 shortTons</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="targetUom" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The target unit of measure for the fuel type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="uomsKey" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The key associated with a unit of measure for the fuel type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogCategory">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the grouping of individual catalog items in Service Catalog.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogcategory.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="image" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of a content document to be displayed in the Service Catalog for this category.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates if a catalog category is active.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value. This value currently has no impact.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The primary label for the catalog category record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parentCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If provided, the name of another SvcCatalogCategory that this category should appear under. The parent category in this field can’t have its own parent category. Categories can’t have more than one level of nesting.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Displays a set order for catalog category entities.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogCategoryItem">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the assignment of this service to a category within the Service Catalog.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isPrimaryCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines if the catalog category (svcCatalogCategory) is the primary category for this catalog item. Exactly one category per SvcCatalogItemDef component must set this attribute to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The position of the catalog item relative to other catalog items in the catalog category.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="svcCatalogCategory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The catalog category the catalog item is assigned to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogFulfillFlowItem">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a variable in a fulfillment flow that can accept input. Describes what type of value it accepts.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogfulfillmentflow.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="catalogInputVariable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The FlowVariable the fulfillment flow property represents.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="displayType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The display options available. Values are: Checkbox Date (available in API version 59.0 and later) DateTime (available in API version 59.0 and later) Lookup Number Picklist Queue (available in API version 57.0 and later) Text</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: PropertyDisplayType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isAdditionalQuestionsInputVariable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines if this variable accepts input for all additional questions that were asked to a user. This value can only be true if the displayType for this item is Text. Only one item per SvcCatalogFulfillmentFlow component can set this attribute to true.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines if the field is required for the related fulfillment flow to be executed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The primary label for the fulfillment flow record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectLookupDomain" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of a custom or standard object. If displayType is Lookup or Picklist, this value filters the available options to a specific object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogFulfillmentFlow">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the flow associated with a specific catalog item in the Service Catalog.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogfulfillmentflow.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Free-text description of the fulfillment flow.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flow" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the flow represented by this SvcCatalogFulfillmentFlow.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="icon" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the details of an icon.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value. This value currently has no impact.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="items" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of variables in the flow that can accept a value as input.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogFulfillFlowItem[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The primary label for the fulfillment flow record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogItemAttrDetail">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the details for an attribute of an item version. Used for options displayed in picklist or checkbox groups.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isDefault" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Marks the attribute detail as the default. Applicable when the input display type is picklist or checkbox.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Picklist option label when the input type is picklist or checkbox.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Attribute value defined by the catalog builder.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogItemAttribute">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an attribute of a catalog item version. It can be a static input filled by the catalog builder user or additional questions that end users answer at runtime. Available in API version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="inputType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Values are: Attachment Checkbox Currency Date Datetime DisplayText Email IPAddress Integer ListOfBoolean ListOfDouble ListOfInteger ListOfMaps ListOfString Lookup Map MultilineText Number NumericScale Percentage Picklist Queue SingleCheckbox (available in API version 59.0 and later) SinglelineText Text Toggle (available in API version 59.0 and later) URL</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemAttrDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inputVariable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>References the input variable to which the attribute value is forwarded.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines if an answer is required for this question.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A translatable label for rendering the attribute to users.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="maxValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Applicable when the display type is slider.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="minValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Applicable when the display type is slider.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Applicable when the display type is Lookup/Reference.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="object" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A picklist object’s custom API Name. Applies when inputType is set to Picklist.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="options" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The values attached to an attribute of an item version.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemAttrDetail</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Type of the attribute; used to determine if it&apos;s a pre-filled input or questions to ask users. Values are: FulfillmentInput UserQuestion</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemAttrType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Attribute value defined by the catalog builder.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogItemDef">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the entity associated with a specific, individual service available in the Service Catalog.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="apiVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:double">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The API version in which this catalog item was created. The value for this field updates based on the value of fulfillmentFlow. For catalog items created before version 57.0, the value for this field is null. Available in version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: double</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="catalogFilterCriteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The eligibility rule associated with a catalog item. Eligibility rules customize access to catalog items for different audiences, based on the User object. Available in API version 59.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemDefFiltrCrit[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="categories" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of catalog categories that contain this catalog item.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogCategoryItem[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataCategories" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of data categories for this catalog item. Available in API version 59.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemDefDataCategorySelection[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Description of the catalog item.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flow" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The screen flow associated with the catalog item. Available in API version 53.0 to 58.0.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fulfillmentFlow" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the related SvcCatalogFulfillmentFlow, which represents the flow associated with a specific catalog item in the Service Catalog. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="image" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of a content document to be displayed in the Service Catalog for this item.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inputs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents attributes of a catalog item version. Available in API version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SvcCatalogItemAttribute[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="internalNotes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Intended to describe what the catalog item does and its implementation. That value is meant for other catalog builders.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isAvailableToAllCustomers" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Controls catalog item access for internal users. To share with all internal users, set the value to True. This value corresponds to the Allow Access for All Users option for Internal Access in the Catalog Item Builder. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isFeatured" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Determines if the catalog item is part of the featured catalog items.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isGuestAccessible" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Controls catalog item access for guest users. To share with guests, set the value to True. This value corresponds to Guest Visibility option for External Access in the Catalog Item Builder. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value. This value has no impact.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The primary label for the catalog item record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sharedTo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Describes how the catalog item is shared across multiple catalog categories. SvcCatalogItemDef only supports sharing with groups.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SharedTo</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="status" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Displays the publishing status of a catalog item. Values are: Deprecated Draft PendingChanges Published</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: PublishStatusType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogItemDefDataCategorySelection">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a list of data categories for this catalog item. This subtype is available in API version 59.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="category" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>API name of a data category.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="categoryGroup" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>API Name of a data category group.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SvcCatalogItemDefFiltrCrit">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the association of an eligibility rule with a catalog item. Eligibility rules customize access to catalog items for different audiences, based on the User object. Available in version 59.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_svccatalogitemdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="svcCatalogFilterCriteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the associated catalogFilerCriteria eligibility filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SynonymDictionary">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a set of synonym groups, which are groups of words or phrases that are treated as equivalent in users’ searches. You can define synonym groups to optimize search results for acronyms, variations of product names, and other terminology unique to your organization.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_synonymdictionary.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="groups" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The synonym groups defined in this dictionary.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SynonymGroup</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether this component is protected (true) or not (false). Protected components cannot be linked to or referenced by components created in the installing organization.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the display name of the synonym dictionary.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="SynonymGroup">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a group of synonymous words or phrases.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_synonymdictionary.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="languages" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the languages the synonym group applies to. If synonyms are specific to a single language, specify only that language. If the synonyms apply to multiple languages, specify multiple languages for one synonym group.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Language</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="terms" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A word or phrase synonymous with other terms in the group. Maximum of 50 characters. Minimum of two terms per group.Synonym groups are symmetric, which means that if oranges and apples are defined in a synonym group, a search for oranges will return a match for apples, and vice versa for a search for apples.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TabLimitConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the maximum number of primary tabs and subtabs allowed in one Salesforce console session. Required if enableTabLimits is true. Available in API version 36.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customapplication.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="maxNumberOfPrimaryTabs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum number of primary tabs allowed in one console session. Valid values are: 5 10 20 30</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="maxNumberOfSubTabs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum number of subtabs allowed in one console session. Valid values are: 5 10 15</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Table_1_Fields">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_ocrtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="targetObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object to which information from a form is mapped.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="targetObjectRecordType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The developer name of the record type of the target object. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Table_2_Fields">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_ocrtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of mapping. Available in API version 56.0 and later.Valid values are: FormField TableColumn The default value is FormField.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: OcrMappingType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Table_3_Fields">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_ocrtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="cellColumnNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The column number in the item with the cell storing this field’s value. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="cellColumnSpanValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The number of columns that span the cell storing this field’s value. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="cellRowNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The row number in the item with the cell storing this field’s value. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="cellRowSpanValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The number of rows that span the cell storing this field’s value. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isAutoExtractedValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the key is automatically extracted (true) or not (false). Available in API version 57.0 and later.This field helps to distinguish auto-extracted keys from manual ones.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="keyContent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The content in a particular area of the form, representing the field that is extracted by OCR.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ocrSampleDocument" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The associated OCR sample document is used as a reference while extracting and mapping information from a customer form.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ocrSampleDocumentPage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A collection of fields that define a page in the OCR sample document.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ocrSampleDocumentPageItem" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A reference to the item on the sample document page containing this field&apos;s value. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: OcrSampleDocumentPageItem</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Table_4_Fields">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_ocrtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="hasHeader" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the OCR sample document page item has a header (true) or not (false). The default value is false. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sequenceNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The sequence number of the item on an OCR sample document page with multiple items. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="title" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The title of the OCR sample document page item. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of OCR sample document page item. Valid value is TABLE. Available in API version 56.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ItemType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Table_5_Fields">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_ocrtemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="ocrSampleDocument" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The associated OCR sample document is used as a reference while extracting and mapping information from a customer form.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a territory.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="accountAccessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether users in this territory can access accounts that are assigned to this territory and are otherwise inaccessible. Valid values are: Read Edit All If your organization’s sharing model for accounts is Public Read/Write, valid values are only Edit and All. If no value is set for this field, this field value uses the default access level that is specified in the Manage Territory page in Setup. This field is available in API version 31.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The unique identifier for API access. The fullName can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters. It must be unique, begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. This field is inherited from the Metadata component. Corresponds to Territory Name in the user interface.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parentTerritory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The territory above this territory in the territory hierarchy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a sales territory. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field. Available if Sales Territories has been enabled.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="accountAccessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether users in this territory can access accounts that are assigned to this territory and are otherwise inaccessible. Valid values are: Read Edit All If your organization’s sharing model for accounts is Public Read/Write, valid values are only Edit and All. If no value is set for this field, this field value uses the default access level that is specified in Territory2Settings as permitted by the organization’s sharing settings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="caseAccessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether users in this territory can access cases that are assigned to this territory and are otherwise inaccessible. Valid values are: None Read Edit Specify no value if your organization’s sharing model for cases/opportunities is Public Read/Write. If no value is set for this field, this field value uses the default access level that is specified in Territory2Settings as permitted by the organization’s sharing settings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="contactAccessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether users in this territory can access contacts that are assigned to this territory and are otherwise inaccessible. Valid values are: None Read Edit Specify no value if your organization’s sharing model for contacts is Public Read/Write or Controlled By Parent.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the territory.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The user interface label for the territory.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectAccessLevels" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents the user access levels of an object associated to a territory. Available in API version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Territory2AccessLevel[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="opportunityAccessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies whether users in this territory can access opportunities that are assigned to this territory and are otherwise inaccessible. Valid values are: None Read Edit Specify no value if your organization’s sharing model for cases/opportunities is Public Read/Write. If no value is set for this field, this field value uses the default access level that is specified in Territory2Settings as permitted by the organization’s sharing settings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parentTerritory" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the territory’s parent. When you specify the parent territory, use the developer name. Do not use the “fully qualified” name. Custom fields with no values are retrieved with values of type: &lt;value xsi:nil=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;. You can also use &lt;value xsi:nil=&quot;true&quot;/&gt; syntax to remove existing values in custom fields.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ruleAssociations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Represents an object assignment rule and its association to a territory. Use the developer name of the rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Territory2RuleAssociation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="territory2Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The territory type that the territory belongs to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2AccessLevel">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the association of an object access level to a territory. Available in API version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="accessLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Valid values are: Read Edit Transfer All If your organization’s sharing model for accounts is Public Read/Write, valid values are only Edit and All. If no value is set for this field, this field value uses the default access level that is specified in Territory2Settings as permitted by the organization’s sharing settings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of object associated to the territory. For example, Lead.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2Model">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a territory model in Sales Territories. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.Available if Sales Territories has been enabled.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2model.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description for the territory model.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The user interface label for the territory model.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2Rule">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata associated with a territory assignment rule associated with an object, such as Account. Available if Sales Territories has been enabled.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2rule.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the rule is active (true) or inactive (false). Via the API, active rules run automatically when object records are created and edited. The exception is when the value of the IsExcludedFromRealign field on an object record is true, which prevents record assignment rules from evaluating that record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="booleanFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An advanced filter condition. For example: (1 AND 2) OR 3. Numbering must start at 1 and must be contiguous.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The user interface label for the rule.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="objectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object that the rule is defined for. For API version 32.0, the only available object is Account.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ruleItems" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The items that define a rule’s the selection criteria, such as Billing State equals California.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: Territory2RuleItem</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2RuleAssociation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the association of an object assignment rule to a territory. Available in API version 32.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="inherited" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the rule is inherited from a parent territory (true) or local to the current territory (false).Rule inheritance flows from the parent territory where the rule is created to the rule’s descendent territories, if any, in the territory model hierarchy. A local rule is created within a single territory and affects that territory only.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ruleName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of a rule associated with the territory. It isn’t necessary to fully qualify ruleName because Metadata API assumes that the rule belongs to the same model as the territory.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2RuleItem">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the association of a rule item to a rule. Available in API version 32.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2rule.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="operation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The criterion to apply for the rule item. For example: equals or starts with. Valid values are: equals notEqual lessThan greaterThan lessOrEqual greaterOrEqual contains notContain startsWith includes excludes within (DISTANCE criteria only)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FilterOperation (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The field value or values to evaluate. For example: if the field is Billing ZIP/Postal Code, a value could be 94105.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Territory2Type">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the metadata for a category of territories in Sales Territories. Every Territory2 must have a Territory2Type. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.Available if Sales Territories has been enabled.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_territory2type.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the territory type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The user interface label for the territory type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="priority" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Used for Filter-Based Opportunity Territory Assignment (Pilot in Spring ’15 / Metadata API version 33). Lets you specify a priority for a territory type. For opportunity assignments, the filter examines all territories assigned to the account that the opportunity is assigned to. The account-assigned territory whose territory type priority is highest is then assigned to the opportunity. The priority field value on each territory type must be unique. Further, if there are multiple territories with the same territory type, and therefore the same priority, assigned to the account, no territory is not assigned to the opportunity.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TimeSheetTemplate">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a template for creating time sheets in Field Service. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_timesheettemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the time sheet template is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The time sheet template&apos;s description.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="frequency" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Defines the frequency of the time sheet creation period. One of the following values: Daily Weekly EveryTwoWeeks TwiceAMonth Monthly</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TimeSheetFrequency (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The name of the time sheet template.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="startDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:date">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The date when the time sheet takes effect.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: date</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="timeSheetTemplateAssignments" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of profiles that the template is assigned to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TimeSheetTemplateAssignment</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="workWeekEndDay" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The end day of the template&apos;s work week. One of the following values: Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Sunday</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DaysOfWeek (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="workWeekStartDay" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The start day of the template&apos;s work week. One of the following values: Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Sunday</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DaysOfWeek (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TimeSheetTemplateAssignment">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Returns a quick action that’s associated with an EmbeddedServiceLiveAgent setup. The quick action includes the pre-chat form fields that the embedded chat window displays and shows the order in which the fields are displayed.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_timesheettemplate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="assignedTo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The IDs of the user profiles that a time sheet template is assigned to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TimelineObjectDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the container that stores the details of a timeline configuration. You can use this resource with Salesforce objects to see their records&apos; related events in a linear time-sorted view.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_timelineobjectdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="baseObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object on which a timeline is based. Information displayed in a timeline comes from objects that are related to the base object. The base object can be a Salesforce object or custom object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="definition" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The timeline definition in JSON format.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the timeline is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The user interface label of the timeline object definition record.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TopicsForObjects">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the ability to assign topics to objects or to remove topic assignments.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_topicsforobjects.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableTopics" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. When true, indicates whether users can assign topics or remove topic assignments. When false, users can’t assign or remove topics.Upon org creation, this value is true for the following objects: Account Asset Campaign Case Contact Content Document Contract Event Lead Opportunity Order Solution Task For all remaining standard objects and custom objects, the default is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="entityApiName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the object’s API name for enabling topics.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TouchMobileSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>These fields are removed in API version 46.0. Salesforce Touch has been upgraded to the Salesforce mobile app.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_mobilesettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableTouchBrowserIPad" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether your organization has the Salesforce Touch mobile browser app enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enableTouchAppIPad" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether your organization has the Salesforce Touch downloadable app enabled (true) or not (false)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TransactionSecurityAction">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Describes the action to take when the matching Transaction Security policy is triggered.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_transactionsecurity.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="block" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, the requested operation is blocked. This action only applies to Login and AccessResource events.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="endSession" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Legacy Transaction Security only. If true, a current session must be closed before a new session can be started. This action only applies to Login events. As of Summer &apos;20, Legacy Transaction Security is a retired feature in all Salesforce orgs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="freezeUser" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Legacy Transaction Security only. If true, the user that triggered the policy is frozen. This action only applies to Chatter resources for Entity events. As of Summer &apos;20, Legacy Transaction Security is a retired feature in all Salesforce orgs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="notifications" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies how to notify the Salesforce administrator when the action is triggered. There can be none, one, or multiple notifications.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TransactionSecurityNotification[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="twoFactorAuthentication" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, multi-factor authentication (MFA) is required for a higher level of access before the requested operation can continue. This action only applies to Login and AccessResource events. Multi-factor authentication was formerly called two-factor authentication.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TransactionSecurityNotification">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Describes who to notify and how to notify them when the matching Transaction Security policy is triggered.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_transactionsecurity.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="inApp" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>True if an in-app notification is selected.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sendEmail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>True if an email notification is selected.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="user" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The user to receive the notification.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="TransactionSecurityPolicy">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a transaction security policy definition. Transaction security policies give you a way to look through events in your organization and specify actions to take when certain combinations occur.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_transactionsecurity.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="action" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Describes the action to take when the matching Transaction Security policy is triggered.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TransactionSecurityAction</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="active" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. If true, the policy is enabled and actively monitors its event.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="apexClass" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required for Apex-based policies, and optional for all other policies. The name of the class that implements the TxnSecurity.PolicyCondition or TxnSecurity.EventCondition interface for this policy. Available in API version 46.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="blockMessage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The custom message sent to a user when a policy blocks their action. Used in Real-Time Event Monitoring only. Maximum of 1000 characters. This field is null when the default message option is selected in the UI. Available only when eventName is set to ApiEvent, ListViewEvent, BulkApiResultEventStore, or ReportEvent. Available in API version 49.0 and later. Include org- or policy-specific information in your custom message, such as the name of the responsible administrator or the business unit. Be careful about what you include. Too much information on how the policy was designed. can aid a malicious user. Two-factor authentication (2FA) isn’t supported in Lightning Experience, so events like ListView and ReportEvent are upgraded to Block in Lightning. Custom messages aren’t translatable.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customEmailContent" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The administrator-created custom email content sent when a policy is triggered. Used in Real-Time Event Monitoring only. Maximum of 1333 characters. This field is null when the Custom Email Content setting is selected in the UI but no message content is entered. Available in API version 54.0 and later.Custom messages aren’t translatable.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description of the policy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>This unique name prevents conflicts with other policies that have the same masterLabel. This name can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters, and must be unique in your org. It must begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. Only users with View DeveloperName OR View Setup and Configuration permission can view, group, sort, and filter this field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="eventName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Real-Time Event Monitoring only. Indicates the name of the event the policy monitors. This field is available in API 45.0 and later. Valid values are: ApiEvent—Tracks these user-initiated read-only API calls: query(), queryMore(), and count(). Captures API requests through SOAP API and Bulk API for the Enterprise and Partner WSDLs. Tooling API calls and API calls originating from a Salesforce mobile app aren’t captured. ApiAnomalyEventStore—Tracks anomalies in how users make API calls. ApiAnomalyEventStore is an object that stores the event data of ApiAnomalyEvent. This object is available in API version 50.0 and later. BulkApiResultEventStore—Tracks when a user downloads the results of a Bulk API request. BulkApiResultEventStore is a big object that stores the event data of BulkApiResultEvent. This object is available in API version 50.0 and later. CredentialStuffingEventStore—Tracks when a user successfully logs into Salesforce during an identified credential stuffing attack. Credential stuffing refers to large-scale automated login requests using stolen user credentials.This value is available in API version 49.0 and later. FileEventStore (beta)—Tracks when a user downloads, previews, or uploads a file. FileEventStore is a big object that stores the event data of FileEvent. This object is available in API version 57.0 and later. GuestUserAnomalyEventStore—Tracks data access anomalies that are caused by guest user permission misconfiguration. This object is available in API version 60.0 and later. ListViewEvent—Tracks when users access data with list views using Lightning Experience, Salesforce Classic, or the API. It doesn’t track list views of Setup entities. LoginAsEvent—Tracks the login activity of admins who log in to Salesforce as other users. This object is available in API version 46.0 and later. LoginEvent—LoginEvent tracks the login activity of users who log in to Salesforce. PermissionSetEventStore —Tracks changes to permission sets and permission set groups. ReportAnomalyEventStore—Tracks anomalies in how users run or export reports, including unsaved reports. This value is available in API version 49.0 and later. ReportEvent—Tracks when reports are run in your org. SessionHijackingEventStore—Tracks when unauthorized users gain ownership of a Salesforce user’s session with a stolen session identifier. To detect such an event, Salesforce evaluates how significantly a user’s current browser fingerprint diverges from the previously known fingerprint using a probabilistically inferred significance of change. Available in API version 49.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TransactionSecurityEventName (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="eventType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Legacy Transaction Security only. Required for Apex-based policies, and optional for all other policies. Indicates which type of event is being monitored. Valid values are: AccessResource—Notifies you when the selected resource has been accessed. AuditTrail—Reserved for future use. DataExport—Notifies you when the selected object type has been exported using the Data Loader API client. Entity—Notifies you on use of an object type such as an authentication provider or Chatter comment. Login—Notifies you when a user logs in. As of Summer &apos;20, Legacy Transaction Security is a retired feature in all Salesforce orgs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: MonitoredEvents (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="executionUser" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Legacy Transaction Security only. The name or ID of an active user who is assigned the Modify All Data and View Setup user permissions. As of Summer &apos;20, Legacy Transaction Security is a retired feature in all Salesforce orgs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flowId" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required only for policies of type CustomConditionBuilderPolicy. The ID of the Flow object that contains the logic the Condition Builder transaction security policy. Available in API version 46.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The label for this object. This display value is the internal label that is’t translated. Where possible, we changed noninclusive terms to align with our company value of Equality. We maintained certain terms to avoid any effect on customer implementations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="resourceName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Used in Legacy Transaction Security only. Required for Apex-based policies, and optional for all other policies. A resource used to narrow down the conditions under which the policy triggers. For example, with a DataExport event, you can select a resource Lead to specifically monitor export activity occurring on your Lead entities. The resources available depend on the Event Type field. The following valid resources are grouped by event type. AccessResource—ConnectedApplication, Reports DataExport—Account, Case, Contact, Lead, Opportunity Entity—AuthProvider, ChatterMessage, FeedComment, FeedItem, Idea, Question Login—LoginHistory As of Summer &apos;20, Legacy Transaction Security is a retired feature in all Salesforce orgs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of validation that the policy uses. The valid values are: CustomApexPolicy— Created with Apex editor. CustomConditionBuilderPolicy— Created with Condition Builder. The default value is CustomApexPolicy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: TxnSecurityPolicyType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="Translations">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Metadata type that enables work with translations for various supported languages. The ability to translate component labels is part of the Translation Workbench.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_translations.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="bots" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of bot translations. Available in API version 53.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: BotTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customApplications" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of custom application translations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomApplicationTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customLabels" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of custom label translations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomLabelTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customPageWebLinks" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of translations for web links defined in a home page component.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomPageWebLinkTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="customTabs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of custom tab translations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: CustomTabTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flowDefinitions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of flow translations.Only Flow and AutolaunchedFlow types are supported for translation. This field is available in API version 41.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FlowDefinitionTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="fullName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The language code. For example, de for German.Inherited from Metadata, this field is defined in the WSDL for this metadata type. It must be specified when creating, updating, or deleting. For an example of this field specified for a call, see createMetadata().</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="globalPicklists" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of global picklist translations. A global picklist’s value set is inherited by all the custom picklist fields that are based on it. This field is available in API version 37.0 only and is removed from later versions.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: GlobalPicklistTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="pipelineInspMetricConfigs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of translations of Pipeline Inspection forecast category metric settings. This field is available in API version 57.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: PipelineInspMetricConfigTranslation</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="prompts" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of In-App Guidance prompt translations. This field is available in API version 48.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: PromptTranslation</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="quickActions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of global rather than object-specific quick actions.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: GlobalQuickActionTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="reportTypes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of report type translations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ReportTypeTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="scontrols" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of s-control translations.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ScontrolTranslation[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UIObjectRelationConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the admin-created configuration of the object relation UI component.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiobjectrelationconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="contextObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object that provides the context for this object relation configuration.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="contextObjectRecordType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The record type of the context object for this configuration, if applicable.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="indirectRelationshipObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For indirect relationships, the junction object representing the relationship between the related object and its context object.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the configuration is active (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Label for the UIObjectRelationConfig. In the UI, this field is UI Object Relation Config.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relatedObject" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object containing the data that this object relation configuration displays.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relatedObjectRecordType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The record type of the related object for this configuration.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="relationshipType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A string indicating the type of relationship between the related object and context object.Valid values are: Direct Indirect InverseDirect Self</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: ObjectRelationshipType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UIObjectRelationFieldConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a configuration for a single row of content on a specific object relation configuration.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiobjectrelationconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="displayLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A string containing the user-defined label for this field, to be displayed on each object relation of this type.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="queryText" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A case-insensitive template query for generating the content in this field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rowOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Determines the top-to-bottom display order of this field on the object relation UI.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UiFormatSpecification">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A single rule in the ruleset.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiformatspecificationset.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="formatProperties" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The properties for a given formatType in JSON format.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="formatType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of conditional formatting associated with the field when the rule evaluates to true. Values are: ICON</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FormatType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="order" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A numerical value representing the conditional formatting rule’s position in the evaluation order.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="visibilityRule" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A set of one or more filters that define the conditions under which the conditional formatting appears on the field.If the visibility rule evaluates to true, the formatting displays on the field. If false, it doesn’t display. If this field is null, the formatting displays by default.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UiFormulaRule</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UiFormatSpecificationSet">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a set of rules that define the style and visibility of conditional field formatting on Dynamic Forms-enabled Lightning page field instances.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiformatspecificationset.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="formatType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of conditional formatting associated with the field. Values are: ICON</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: FormatType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The label for the conditional formatting ruleset, which displays in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sobjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The object the ruleset is associated with.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="uiFormatSpecifications" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The list of rules contained in the ruleset.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UiFormatSpecification[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UiFormulaCriterion">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A single filter that when evaluated, helps define conditional formatting visibility on a Dynamic Forms-enabled Lightning page field instance.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiformatspecificationset.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="leftValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The field upon which the filter is based. For example, AMOUNT.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="operator" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Defines the operator used to filter the data. Valid values are: CONTAINS EQUAL NE—not equal GT—greater than GE—greater than or equal LE—less than or equal LT—less than</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="rightValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The value by which you want to evaluate the formatting visibility. For example, 1000000.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UiFormulaRule">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>A set of one or more filters that define the conditions under which conditional field formatting displays on a Dynamic Forms-enabled Lightning page field instance. For example, you could construct a filter that causes conditional formatting to display only when the Amount field is greater than $1,000,000.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uiformatspecificationset.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="booleanFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies advanced filter conditions such as 1 AND 2.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="criteria" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>List of one or more filters that, when evaluated, determine conditional field formatting visibility.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UiFormulaCriterion[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UiPreviewMessageTabDef">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the registration of a custom Marketing Cloud Preview and Test modal tab, created using custom Lightning web components. You can register and show multiple tabs in the Preview and Test experience.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_uipreviewmessagetabdef.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the tab is enabled and is customer controlled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the configuration is protected (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Label for the tab.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lightningComponentDef" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The customer-created Lightning web component that displays in the Preview and Test tabs.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportedChannel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A string indicating the type of channel.Values are: Email Sms WhatsApp</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: SupportedChannel (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="tabName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The case-sensitive, user-defined label displayed as the name of the tab. Maximum length is 255 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserAccessPolicy">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a user access policy.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_useraccesspolicy.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="booleanFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The logic that determines how your user criteria filters are applied in the user access policy. For example, if you have two user access policy filters with the sortOrder equal to 1 and 2, respectively, the booleanFilter can be 1 AND 2 or 1 OR 2.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Description of the user access policy.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isProtected" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An auto-generated value that doesn’t impact the behavior of the metadata type. The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name for the user access policy, which is defined when the user access policy is created.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="order" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates the order for which active policy is applied when a user meets the criteria for multiple policies. Must be an integer from 0 to 10,000. Only the active policy with the lowest order value is applied. This field is required only if the status field is set to Active. Available in API version 61.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="status" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The status of the user access policy. Values are: Active Completed Design Failed Migrate Testing Updating If you deploy a policy with a status of Active, the status is changed to Design. A Salesforce admin can then set the status to Active by automating the policy in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyStatus (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="triggerType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The type of user record trigger for which this user access policy runs. Values are: Create—The user access policy runs when a user who matches the policy criteria is created. CreateAndUpdate—The user access policy runs when a user who matches the policy criteria is either created or updated. Update—The user access policy runs when a user who matches the policy criteria is updated.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyTriggerType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userAccessPolicyActions" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The actions applied by the user access policy to grant access to or revoke access from an access mechanism.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyAction[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userAccessPolicyFilters" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The filters used to define the users that the user access policy is applied to.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyFilter[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserAccessPolicyAction">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an action applied by a user access policy.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_useraccesspolicy.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="action" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates whether the user access policy grants or revokes the target access mechanism. Values are: Grant Revoke</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyActionType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="target" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Developer name of the access mechanism that the user access policy applies.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of access mechanism that the user access policy applies. Values are: Group PackageLicense PermissionSet PermissionSetGroup PermissionSetLicense Queue</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyActionTargetType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserAccessPolicyFilter">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a user criteria filter for a user access policy.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_useraccesspolicy.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="columnName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If type is set to User, this is the user field that your user criteria filter is based on. If you set type to any value other than User, then this field isn’t used.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="operation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The operator of the user criteria filter. Values are: equals equalsIgnoreCase—Available in API version 59.0 and later. in— Available in API version 58.0 and later. includes—Available in API version 59.0 and later. notEquals Select in if you want to reference multiple profiles or roles in the same user criteria filter via the target field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyFilterOperation (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="sortOrder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The numeric reference used to identify the specific user criteria filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="target" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. If type is set to User, then set this field to User as well. If type is set to any other value, then set this field to the developer name of the specific resource used in the user criteria filter.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of resource that the user criteria filter is based on. Values are: Group PackageLicense PermissionSet PermissionSetGroup PermissionSetLicense Profile Queue User UserRole</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: UserAccessPolicyFilterTargetType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If type is set to User, this field is the value of the user field specified in columnName that your user filter is operating on. If you set type to any value other than User, then this field isn’t used.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserAuthCertificate">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a PEM-encoded user certificate. These certificates are associated with a user, and externally uploaded. The uploaded certificate is used to authenticate the user.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_userauthcertificate.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required: The name of the certificate with an underscore between words.Only users with View DeveloperName OR View Setup and Configuration permission can view, group, sort, and filter this field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="expirationDate" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:dateTime">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The date on which the certificate expires.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: dateTime</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A user-friendly name that you create for the certificate. Limited to 64 characters.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="serialNumber" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The serial number for the certificate.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="user" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required: The user’s name.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserCriteria">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the member criteria to use in Experience Cloud site moderation rules. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field..</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_usercriteria.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="creationAgeInSeconds" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, includes only users that were created within a specific time frame.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The description of the user criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="lastChatterActivityAgeInSeconds" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If specified, includes only members that have posted or commented in the Experience Cloud site within a specific time frame.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Name of the user criteria.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userTypes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The member type to use in moderation rules. Valid values are: Internal Customer Partner</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: NetworkUserType enumeration ( of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="UserProvisioningConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents information to use during a user provisioning request flow, such as the attributes for an update. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_userprovisioningconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="approvalRequired" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether approvals are required for provisioning users for the associated connected app. If the value is null, no approval is required.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="connectedApp" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ID of the connected app for which users are being provisioned.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enabled" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether user provisioning is enabled for the associated connected app (true) or not (false). Default setting is false.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="enabledOperations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Lists the operations, as comma-separated values, that create a user provisioning request for the associated connected app. Allowed values are: Create Update EnableAndDisable (activation and deactivation) SuspendAndRestore (freeze and unfreeze)</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="flow" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>User Provisioning flow type which includes a reference to the Apex UserProvisioningPlugin class. The flow calls the third-party service’s API to manage user account provisioning on that system.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The primary label for this object. This value is the internal label that doesn’t get translated.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="namedCredential" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The Salesforce ID of the named credential that’s used for a request. The named credential identifies the third-party system and the third-party authentication settings.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="notes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Serves as a place for admins to add any additional information about the configuration. This field is for internal reference only, and is not used by any process.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="onUpdateAttributes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Lists the user attributes, as comma-separated values, that generate a user provisioning request during an update.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="reconFilter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>When collecting and analyzing users on a third-party system, the plug-in uses this filter to limit the scope of the collection.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="userAccountMapping" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Stores the attributes used to link the Salesforce user to the account on the third-party system, in JSON format. For example:</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="ValueTranslation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>The original value name and the translated value name in a translated global value set.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_globalvaluesettranslation.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The original (untranslated) name of a value in a global value set. Each valueTranslation has a masterLabel paired with its translation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="translation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The translated name of a value in a translated global value set.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
    <xsd:attribute name="fqn" type="xsd:string"/>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="VirtualVisitConfig">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an external video provider configuration, which relays events from Salesforce to the provider.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_virtualvisitconfig.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="comprehendServiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Specifies the type of service used to convert speech into text or to analyze the converted speech text.Valid values are: ComprehendMedicalService ComprehendService</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: VirtualVisitComprehendServiceType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="developerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The unique name of the object in the API. This name can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters, and must be unique in your org. It must begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores. In managed packages, this field prevents naming conflicts on package installations. With this field, a developer can change the object’s name in a managed package and the changes are reflected in a subscriber’s organization. Label is Record Type Name. This field is automatically generated, but you can supply your own value if you create the record using the API.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="experienceCloudSiteUrl" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The URL of the Digital Experience site where the Video Call component is available to portal or guest users.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalMsgServiceIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For internal use only.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalRoleIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The ID of the role that&apos;s used to allow users to join a video call and to grant them temporary access to certain functions needed to participate in the call.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalUserIdentifier" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>For internal use only.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
